6Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/f808fd55163f70622e316058bc6986e03ae6b865/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:52:05Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:24:08Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"improvement(dashboard): give the stacked charts back the height the chrome took\n\nFully restacked, the inventory cell and the two chart panels share one column\nheight, so every line of chrome above a chart is a line of chart lost. Three\nchanges, all confined to the stacked step:\n\n- each service group becomes a single row with its heading inline, instead of\n  a heading line above the tallest group''s four items;\n- the panels drop their desktop gap and bottom padding between the title and\n  the charts;\n- the context bar''s trailing padding goes, so the Advanced Metrics button\n  lines up with the right edge of the panels below it.","tree":{"sha":"d12299bb85089ed5ccc8a424ba39f6e79b647178","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/trees/d12299bb85089ed5ccc8a424ba39f6e79b647178"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/commits/f808fd55163f70622e316058bc6986e03ae6b865","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.c