https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/5ac2b35c9f66292cd47a60648d79daee669f87e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:03:37Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:03:37Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"message":"chore(changelog): drop a sentence this branch makes untrue (MK8S-157)\n\nThe entry MK8S-395 left behind ends with \"Nothing fills that directory yet,\nso the timer is a no-op on a fresh cluster until the cache provisioning\nlands\". That was true when it was written. This branch is the cache\nprovisioning, and both ship in the same release, so a reader of the release\nnotes would be told the timer does nothing while it is importing at every\nbootstrap.\n\nEdited by hand rather than through the `/changie` comment that produced it:\n#5109 is merged, so its workflow can no longer regenerate the fragment.","tree":{"sha":"d44c929549ec9f96aba2074da8d37014f11d9669","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/trees/d44c929549ec9f96aba2074da8d37014f11d9669"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/commits/5ac2b35c9f66292cd47a60648d79daee669f87e9","verification":{"payload":"tree d44c929549ec9f96aba2074da8d37014f11d9669\nparent 4b9652894ac38b2867a92c744d314a72f2f78ee1\nauthor Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788879817 +0200\ncommitter Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788879817 +0200\n\nchore(changelog): drop a sentence this branch makes untrue (MK8S-157)\n\nThe entry MK8S-395 left behind ends with \"Nothing fills that directory yet,\nso the timer is a no-op on a fresh cluster until the cache provisioning\nlands\". That was true when it was written. This branch is the cache\nprovisioning, and both ship in the same release, so a reader of the release\nnotes would be told the timer does nothing while it is importing at every\nbootstrap.\n\nEdited by hand rather than through the `/changie` comment that produced it:\n#5109 is merged, so its workflow can no longer regenerate the fragment.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQQBeSVJcD2ZrbqXtLF0uKJwZUOQDwUCaqAjyQAKCRB0uKJwZUOQ\nD/VPAQCQid4CBbmhdD6qycNNaTSjFoxxGQtdsLjkH49ZU9ALaQD/ao/a+HkHO0Xk\n45zG5qVIkCUpDpIGuiMsS0dzqCqzsAU=\n=CcSD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T15:03:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/5ac2b35c9f66292cd47a60648d79daee669f87e9","node_id":"C_kwDOB3HpytoAKDVhYzJiMzVjOWY2NjI5MmNkNDdhNjA2NDhkNzlkYWVlNjY5Zjg3ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/4b9652894ac38b2867a92c744d314a72f2f78ee1","sha":"4b9652894ac38b2867a92c744d314a72f2f78ee1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/4b9652894ac38b2867a92c744d314a72f2f78ee1"}],"sha":"5ac2b35c9f66292cd47a60648d79daee669f87e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/5ac2b35c9f66292cd47a60648d79daee669f87e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/4b9652894ac38b2867a92c744d314a72f2f78ee1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:47:08Z","email":"ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ezekiel-alexrod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:47:08Z","email":"ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ezekiel-alexrod"},"message":"changelog: The bootstrap node now fills its image cache from the boot cache image shipped on the ISO, before the kubelet starts. The archives it carries are extracted into `/var/lib/image-cache` and imported into containerd right away, so the first node can bring up its static pods with no registry to pull from. Only the control plane variant is provisioned, and only at bootstrap: a node joining the cluster still gets nothing.\n\nAuto-generated-by: changie-add-changelog","tree":{"sha":"20c0c09685ba02e7e06ac706b88f1922a7f43a68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/trees/20c0c09685ba02e7e06ac706b88f1922a7f43a68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/commits/4b9652894ac38b2867a92c744d314a72f2f78ee1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/4b9652894ac38b2867a92c744d314a72f2f78ee1","node_id":"C_kwDOB3HpytoAKDRiOTY1Mjg5NGFjMzhiMjg2N2E5MmM3NDRkMzE0YTcyZjJmNzhlZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/0c338aed8499eded35f2d23dbccc18b0ffc01388","sha":"0c338aed8499eded35f2d23dbccc18b0ffc01388","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/0c338aed8499eded35f2d23dbccc18b0ffc01388"}],"sha":"4b9652894ac38b2867a92c744d314a72f2f78ee1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/4b9652894ac38b2867a92c744d314a72f2f78ee1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/0c338aed8499eded35f2d23dbccc18b0ffc01388/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:18:08Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:32:14Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"message":"feat(salt): fill the image cache at bootstrap (MK8S-157)\n\nThe first node has no registry to pull from and no Kubernetes to run the\nimage cache agent, so its archives come out of the ISO.\n`metalk8s.image-cache.provisioned` extracts them, then runs the preload\nservice once, before the kubelet may start.\n\nThat explicit run is the part worth explaining. The service is\n`Type=oneshot` and its timer fires at boot, then every 10 minutes. Enabling\nthe timer is enough to keep the cache imported over the life of the node,\nbut at bootstrap it has most likely fired already, back when there was\nnothing to import. Waiting for the next firing would let the kubelet start\nwith no images, on a node that cannot reach a registry.\n\nA restart and not a start. The timer may have fired while the archives were\nstill being written, and systemd merges a start request into a start job\nalready in flight: the request would come back happy while the run it joined\nhad listed the directory before the last archives landed.\n\nThe ordering against the kubelet is declared in `roles/bootstrap/local.sls`.\nNot in the formula, because an `_in` requisite only resolves against a state\nin the same run, so declaring it there would make\n`state.sls metalk8s.image-cache.provisioned` fail to compile on its own,\nwhich is both the debug path and what MK8S-394 will reuse. And not in\n`init.sls`, because that is not where the kubelet first starts:\n`bootstrap.sh` applies `metalk8s.roles.internal.early-stage-bootstrap`,\nwhich reaches `local.sls` and `metalk8s.kubernetes.kubelet.standalone` long\nbefore the highstate, so a gate in `init.sls` would have been decorative for\nthe only start that matters. `init.sls` includes `local.sls`, so the\nhighstate is covered too.\n\nThe formula is reached from the bootstrap role only, not from\n`metalk8s.image-cache`, which the node role includes too. A joining node has\nno ISO mounted, and filling its cache is MK8S-394.\n\nThe mount that carries the source is a real requisite now, rather than an\ninclude order two levels up in the role.\n\nOnly the control plane variant is provisioned. The worker and registry\nvariants land with MK8S-380 and MK8S-394, and so does picking a variant from\nthe roles a node holds.","tree":{"sha":"e593cc90c0d9207f45466783a86cf307b17a8d2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/trees/e593cc90c0d9207f45466783a86cf307b17a8d2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/commits/0c338aed8499eded35f2d23dbccc18b0ffc01388","verification":{"payload":"tree e593cc90c0d9207f45466783a86cf307b17a8d2e\nparent 420dcf238ad2a62e4f93f1ebd86b8a701f06d94f\nauthor Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788362288 +0200\ncommitter Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788877934 +0200\n\nfeat(salt): fill the image cache at bootstrap (MK8S-157)\n\nThe first node has no registry to pull from and no Kubernetes to run the\nimage cache agent, so its archives come out of the ISO.\n`metalk8s.image-cache.provisioned` extracts them, then runs the preload\nservice once, before the kubelet may start.\n\nThat explicit run is the part worth explaining. The service is\n`Type=oneshot` and its timer fires at boot, then every 10 minutes. Enabling\nthe timer is enough to keep the cache imported over the life of the node,\nbut at bootstrap it has most likely fired already, back when there was\nnothing to import. Waiting for the next firing would let the kubelet start\nwith no images, on a node that cannot reach a registry.\n\nA restart and not a start. The timer may have fired while the archives were\nstill being written, and systemd merges a start request into a start job\nalready in flight: the request would come back happy while the run it joined\nhad listed the directory before the last archives landed.\n\nThe ordering against the kubelet is declared in `roles/bootstrap/local.sls`.\nNot in the formula, because an `_in` requisite only resolves against a state\nin the same run, so declaring it there would make\n`state.sls metalk8s.image-cache.provisioned` fail to compile on its own,\nwhich is both the debug path and what MK8S-394 will reuse. And not in\n`init.sls`, because that is not where the kubelet first starts:\n`bootstrap.sh` applies `metalk8s.roles.internal.early-stage-bootstrap`,\nwhich reaches `local.sls` and `metalk8s.kubernetes.kubelet.standalone` long\nbefore the highstate, so a gate in `init.sls` would have been decorative for\nthe only start that matters. `init.sls` includes `local.sls`, so the\nhighstate is covered too.\n\nThe formula is reached from the bootstrap role only, not from\n`metalk8s.image-cache`, which the node role includes too. A joining node has\nno ISO mounted, and filling its cache is MK8S-394.\n\nThe mount that carries the source is a real requisite now, rather than an\ninclude order two levels up in the role.\n\nOnly the control plane variant is provisioned. The worker and registry\nvariants land with MK8S-380 and MK8S-394, and so does picking a variant from\nthe roles a node holds.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQQBeSVJcD2ZrbqXtLF0uKJwZUOQDwUCaqAcbgAKCRB0uKJwZUOQ\nD03iAQDdMqqu7iIDwpTN+9C6phwJ+ez+UTTH7f7oejSRlLWkwwD9H7cFRkuDIpB1\n4uv10a1Y0f2PR9nEOIkdJ2+pyqDKiwM=\n=3vH/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T14:46:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/0c338aed8499eded35f2d23dbccc18b0ffc01388","node_id":"C_kwDOB3HpytoAKDBjMzM4YWVkODQ5OWVkZWQzNWYyZDIzZGJjY2MxOGIwZmZjMDEzODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/420dcf238ad2a62e4f93f1ebd86b8a701f06d94f","sha":"420dcf238ad2a62e4f93f1ebd86b8a701f06d94f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/420dcf238ad2a62e4f93f1ebd86b8a701f06d94f"}],"sha":"0c338aed8499eded35f2d23dbccc18b0ffc01388","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/0c338aed8499eded35f2d23dbccc18b0ffc01388"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/420dcf238ad2a62e4f93f1ebd86b8a701f06d94f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:18:06Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:32:14Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"message":"feat(salt): render the image preload configuration from the pillar (MK8S-157)\n\n`containerd-image-preload` reads its cache directory from\n`/etc/sysconfig/containerd-image-preload`, and the states that fill that\ncache read it from the pillar. Left as two independent values they drift:\nsetting `image_cache: {directory: /srv/image-cache}` would have Salt\npopulate one directory while the timer kept importing from the other, both\nreporting success, and no image ever imported.\n\nSo Salt renders the file, from the same values it uses everywhere else. The\npackage ships it as `%config(noreplace)`, which is what makes this safe: RPM\nleaves it alone on an upgrade.\n\nA `require` on the timer rather than a `watch_in`. The service reads its\nenvironment file every time it runs, so a changed directory is picked up on\nthe next tick, and there is no reason to restart a timer that is already\narmed.","tree":{"sha":"40b25a317952b006a4d41e4f0f97258bec09532b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/trees/40b25a317952b006a4d41e4f0f97258bec09532b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/commits/420dcf238ad2a62e4f93f1ebd86b8a701f06d94f","verification":{"payload":"tree 40b25a317952b006a4d41e4f0f97258bec09532b\nparent c6d75213797313608635ca3e5a7e84f9dab87fdd\nauthor Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788362286 +0200\ncommitter Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788877934 +0200\n\nfeat(salt): render the image preload configuration from the pillar (MK8S-157)\n\n`containerd-image-preload` reads its cache directory from\n`/etc/sysconfig/containerd-image-preload`, and the states that fill that\ncache read it from the pillar. Left as two independent values they drift:\nsetting `image_cache: {directory: /srv/image-cache}` would have Salt\npopulate one directory while the timer kept importing from the other, both\nreporting success, and no image ever imported.\n\nSo Salt renders the file, from the same values it uses everywhere else. The\npackage ships it as `%config(noreplace)`, which is what makes this safe: RPM\nleaves it alone on an upgrade.\n\nA `require` on the timer rather than a `watch_in`. The service reads its\nenvironment file every time it runs, so a changed directory is picked up on\nthe next tick, and there is no reason to restart a timer that is already\narmed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQQBeSVJcD2ZrbqXtLF0uKJwZUOQDwUCaqAcbgAKCRB0uKJwZUOQ\nD0AkAP9AIz0i6Lf8EQjMuaJkN9f/E0V9KBY0kWf/PRZq0GSHwgD9EPpT77xmyGD2\nrwe6JLc3EW3hZDT6Zwx/5hW+dOCNYgk=\n=RYIJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T14:46:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/420dcf238ad2a62e4f93f1ebd86b8a701f06d94f","node_id":"C_kwDOB3HpytoAKDQyMGRjZjIzOGFkMmE2MmU0ZjkzZjFlYmQ4NmI4YTcwMWYwNmQ5NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/c6d75213797313608635ca3e5a7e84f9dab87fdd","sha":"c6d75213797313608635ca3e5a7e84f9dab87fdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/c6d75213797313608635ca3e5a7e84f9dab87fdd"}],"sha":"420dcf238ad2a62e4f93f1ebd86b8a701f06d94f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/420dcf238ad2a62e4f93f1ebd86b8a701f06d94f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/c6d75213797313608635ca3e5a7e84f9dab87fdd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:17:55Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:32:14Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"message":"feat(salt): read the archives a boot cache image carries (MK8S-157)\n\nA boot cache image is a carrier and nothing else: built `FROM scratch` with\na single `COPY`, it holds one archive per container image a node of its role\nneeds to boot. `metalk8s_image_cache.provision` reads those archives out of\nthe docker archive and writes them into the cache directory.\n\nThe ticket asked for `ctr images import`, then `ctr images mount`, then a\ncopy. That does work, I checked it against containerd, but it is expensive\non the node that can least afford it. The archive shipped on the ISO is not\ncompressed, so the import writes about 1.1 GB into the content store, and\nthe unpack it performs by default writes about as much again into the\nsnapshotter. Neither is given back by `ctr images rm`: the namespace still\nrefuses to be deleted afterwards, with `must be empty, but it still has\nblobs, snapshots on \"overlayfs\"`. Containerd''s garbage collector reclaims\nthem, whenever it next runs. Reading the archive costs one pass and leaves\nnothing behind, and there is no temporary mount left to unmount when a copy\nfails halfway.\n\nThe headers are walked before anything is written, and the layer is opened\nfor random access rather than as a stream. That buys two things. An image\nthis module refuses is refused whole, rather than leaving behind the prefix\nit had already copied, which the preload script would glob and import as if\nit were a full cache. And on the second run, when every archive is already\nin place, walking the headers seeks over the payload instead of reading\nseveral hundred megabytes off the mounted ISO to throw them away.\n\nEach archive is written under a hidden name, flushed, fsynced, then renamed.\nThe timer reading that directory may fire at any moment, so nothing partial\nmay ever appear under the final name, and the node is mid-install, so the\nbytes have to reach the disk before the name does.\n\nArchives land flat in the cache directory, which is not a new decision. The\npreload script the `containerd-image-preload` package ships globs\n`$IMAGE_CACHE_DIR/*.tar` for provisioning and `*/*.tar` for the agent, and\nthe agent only collects the subdirectories it marked with its sentinel.\nNames are taken as they come, with no re-tagging, because the archives\nalready carry the name the kubelet asks for (MK8S-153).\n\nAn archive already in the cache with the size the image announces is left\nalone, so a second run copies nothing. The same size with different content\ndoes get through that check. The import that follows is what fails loudly,\nand the cold path writes once instead of tracking updates the way the agent\nhas to.","tree":{"sha":"47a476dacdb8d96b6130b8046f89e92011a03ae1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/trees/47a476dacdb8d96b6130b8046f89e92011a03ae1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/commits/c6d75213797313608635ca3e5a7e84f9dab87fdd","verification":{"payload":"tree 47a476dacdb8d96b6130b8046f89e92011a03ae1\nparent b10b268eb0fb890070f3036e45b6e4b12296adca\nauthor Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788362275 +0200\ncommitter Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788877934 +0200\n\nfeat(salt): read the archives a boot cache image carries (MK8S-157)\n\nA boot cache image is a carrier and nothing else: built `FROM scratch` with\na single `COPY`, it holds one archive per container image a node of its role\nneeds to boot. `metalk8s_image_cache.provision` reads those archives out of\nthe docker archive and writes them into the cache directory.\n\nThe ticket asked for `ctr images import`, then `ctr images mount`, then a\ncopy. That does work, I checked it against containerd, but it is expensive\non the node that can least afford it. The archive shipped on the ISO is not\ncompressed, so the import writes about 1.1 GB into the content store, and\nthe unpack it performs by default writes about as much again into the\nsnapshotter. Neither is given back by `ctr images rm`: the namespace still\nrefuses to be deleted afterwards, with `must be empty, but it still has\nblobs, snapshots on \"overlayfs\"`. Containerd''s garbage collector reclaims\nthem, whenever it next runs. Reading the archive costs one pass and leaves\nnothing behind, and there is no temporary mount left to unmount when a copy\nfails halfway.\n\nThe headers are walked before anything is written, and the layer is opened\nfor random access rather than as a stream. That buys two things. An image\nthis module refuses is refused whole, rather than leaving behind the prefix\nit had already copied, which the preload script would glob and import as if\nit were a full cache. And on the second run, when every archive is already\nin place, walking the headers seeks over the payload instead of reading\nseveral hundred megabytes off the mounted ISO to throw them away.\n\nEach archive is written under a hidden name, flushed, fsynced, then renamed.\nThe timer reading that directory may fire at any moment, so nothing partial\nmay ever appear under the final name, and the node is mid-install, so the\nbytes have to reach the disk before the name does.\n\nArchives land flat in the cache directory, which is not a new decision. The\npreload script the `containerd-image-preload` package ships globs\n`$IMAGE_CACHE_DIR/*.tar` for provisioning and `*/*.tar` for the agent, and\nthe agent only collects the subdirectories it marked with its sentinel.\nNames are taken as they come, with no re-tagging, because the archives\nalready carry the name the kubelet asks for (MK8S-153).\n\nAn archive already in the cache with the size the image announces is left\nalone, so a second run copies nothing. The same size with different content\ndoes get through that check. The import that follows is what fails loudly,\nand the cold path writes once instead of tracking updates the way the agent\nhas to.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQQBeSVJcD2ZrbqXtLF0uKJwZUOQDwUCaqAcbgAKCRB0uKJwZUOQ\nD9wxAP0e5/G+JHuqbQSLYcMdb44cY6Os5YjPfkJzXD2iF83qZQEAzTEl/8m+OR61\nOchfaOdHYY8YXN9A+LGS4vwg7ZX0wQg=\n=DcfW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T14:46:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/c6d75213797313608635ca3e5a7e84f9dab87fdd","node_id":"C_kwDOB3HpytoAKGM2ZDc1MjEzNzk3MzEzNjA4NjM1Y2EzZTVhN2U4NGY5ZGFiODdmZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/b10b268eb0fb890070f3036e45b6e4b12296adca","sha":"b10b268eb0fb890070f3036e45b6e4b12296adca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/b10b268eb0fb890070f3036e45b6e4b12296adca"}],"sha":"c6d75213797313608635ca3e5a7e84f9dab87fdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/c6d75213797313608635ca3e5a7e84f9dab87fdd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25904340?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bert-e","id":25904340,"login":"bert-e","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTA0MzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/b10b268eb0fb890070f3036e45b6e4b12296adca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T10:30:16Z","email":"wall_e@scality.com","name":"bert-e"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T10:30:16Z","email":"wall_e@scality.com","name":"bert-e"},"message":"Merge branch ''improvement/MK8S-395-install-and-enable-image-preload'' into q/134.0","tree":{"sha":"8a21babddb2af0d61f3bc193a0a40a840a1a9213","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/trees/8a21babddb2af0d61f3bc193a0a40a840a1a9213"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/commits/b10b268eb0fb890070f3036e45b6e4b12296adca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25904340?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bert-e","id":25904340,"login":"bert-e","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTA0MzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bert-e","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/b10b268eb0fb890070f3036e45b6e4b12296adca","node_id":"C_kwDOB3HpytoAKGIxMGIyNjhlYjBmYjg5MDA3MGYzMDM2ZTQ1YjZlNGIxMjI5NmFkY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/8927c4084ef234552904ac7d104d1a1b191f5d0e","sha":"8927c4084ef234552904ac7d104d1a1b191f5d0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/8927c4084ef234552904ac7d104d1a1b191f5d0e"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/b22a38e11109f70c8a6bf3c393a736eaa4c724e0","sha":"b22a38e11109f70c8a6bf3c393a736eaa4c724e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/b22a38e11109f70c8a6bf3c393a736eaa4c724e0"}],"sha":"b10b268eb0fb890070f3036e45b6e4b12296adca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/b10b268eb0fb890070f3036e45b6e4b12296adca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/b22a38e11109f70c8a6bf3c393a736eaa4c724e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T14:16:30Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T14:16:30Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"message":"fix(tests): let the new sanity steps survive a slow minion\n\n`salt --static` gathers minions with a ping before running the function, and a\nnode busy with post-install work can miss it. The step then failed the scenario\nwith \"no answer from node-2\" on a healthy cluster. Both steps now go through\n`utils.retry`, the way every other assertion in this module does.\n\nThe package check also quotes what a node answered. A minion that could not run\n`pkg.version` returns its error message, which used to be reported as a plain\n\"not installed\" and pointed at a packaging problem that did not exist.","tree":{"sha":"ef16bddb78186ad65e04deb8bf3c4b2f3982a0dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/trees/ef16bddb78186ad65e04deb8bf3c4b2f3982a0dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/git/commits/b22a38e11109f70c8a6bf3c393a736eaa4c724e0","verification":{"payload":"tree ef16bddb78186ad65e04deb8bf3c4b2f3982a0dc\nparent 08d4d184334254e1b2eb5832c4d29743c120174b\nauthor Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788790590 +0200\ncommitter Alex Rodriguez <131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com> 1788790590 +0200\n\nfix(tests): let the new sanity steps survive a slow minion\n\n`salt --static` gathers minions with a ping before running the function, and a\nnode busy with post-install work can miss it. The step then failed the scenario\nwith \"no answer from node-2\" on a healthy cluster. Both steps now go through\n`utils.retry`, the way every other assertion in this module does.\n\nThe package check also quotes what a node answered. A minion that could not run\n`pkg.version` returns its error message, which used to be reported as a plain\n\"not installed\" and pointed at a packaging problem that did not exist.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQQBeSVJcD2ZrbqXtLF0uKJwZUOQDwUCap7HPgAKCRB0uKJwZUOQ\nD1cRAQDWCSxNLF1csyjulIM0FHRgDgdES+fN4h1aTrzHAwy8NgD/XyHMr7dVbTpj\nN5Q2wVIj3+67yegsJbTRHe+rFEZLuQ8=\n=Vhmi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T14:57:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/b22a38e11109f70c8a6bf3c393a736eaa4c724e0","node_id":"C_kwDOB3HpytoAKGIyMmEzOGUxMTEwOWY3MGM4YTZiZjNjMzkzYTczNmVhYTRjNzI0ZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/metalk8s/commit/08d4d184334254e1b2eb5832c4d29743c120174b","sha":"08d4d184334254e1b2eb5832c4d29743c120174b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/08d4d184334254e1b2eb5832c4d29743c120174b"}],"sha":"b22a38e11109f70c8a6bf3c393a736eaa4c724e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/b22a38e11109f70c8a6bf3c393a736eaa4c724e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131964409?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ezekiel-alexrod","id":131964409,"login":"ezekiel-alexrod","node_id":"U_kgDOB92d-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezekiel-alexrod","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/metalk8s/commits/08d4d184334254e1b2eb5832c4d29743c120174b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T13:57:11Z","email":"131964409+ezekiel-alexrod@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Rodriguez"},"comment_count":0,"committ