":"EthanFreestone","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzEwNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/mod-agreements/commits/1964947df0264ca88010c939bfbf0b5ae46ce1e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-05T14:35:11Z","email":"54310740+EthanFreestone@users.noreply.github.com","name":"EthanFreestone"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-05T14:35:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Resource access policies do not protect agreement line creation -- ERM-3862 (#957)\n\n* feat: PolicyControlled Restriction owner mappings\n\nAdded a mapping from each level of the ownership chain in PolicyControlledManager, corresponding to how that level handles a given restriction\n\n(options include pass through to owner, use standalone policies, both, or neither)\n\nAdded test assertion to that effect in PolicyControlledManagerTest\n\n* fix: Undo accidental TODO change, not necessary\n\n* fix: Javadoc failed\n\n* feat(PolicyControlledManager): Add helper functions for getting a particular owner level safely and returning the size of the ownership chain\n\n* feat(RestrictionMapEntry): Enhance builder with fluent accessors and maintain equality/hashcode\n\n* feat(PolicyControlledValidator): Set up Validator class to validate uses of @PolicyControlled\n\nNewly mandatory: resourceIdColumn, resourceIdField and resourceTableName\n\nTest updates to match\n\n* feat(PolicyControlledManager): Ability for PolicyControlledManager to spit out SQL for obtaining a given owner level''s id\n\n* docs(PolicyControlledManager): javadoc extension\n\n* feat(AccessPolicyAwareController): !WIP! Set up ownership chain parsing for getPolicySql\n\n* fix(session): Fix session management to marry up to changes on master\n\n* refactor: Start ownership level at 0 instead of -1 for the policyControlledManager ownership chain\n\nI _think_ this is no longer needed thanks to the SQL creation built into the policyControlledManager\n\n* fix: Previous changes had broken the CLAIM operation\n\nThis does NOT introduce the changes required to have standalone CLAIM policies on every level, only to fix what had been previously broken\n\n* chore: Include a clause label in the SQL generated by AcquisitionUnitPolicySubquery\n\nALSO... note that this is creating SQL via DIRECT string SQL injection. It must be INCREDIBLY careful to only set these parameters via trusted code.\n\nUnfortunately this is somewhat unavoidable when trying to set up dynamic SQL. Attempt to mitigate by avoiding any dodgy SQL characters (hopefully)\n\n* fix: More SQL injection protection -- now allows for hibernate style {alias} as well\n\n* fix: More SQL injection protection -- now allows for hibernate style {alias} as well\n\n* feat: Swap the building of SQL up the hierarchy over to an object oriented methodology\n\n* refactor: Move the bulk of the RestrictionTree creation logic and subquery fetching logic at each level over to core components\n\n* refactor: Set up RestrictionTree skeleton which lives on the PolicyControlledManager\n\nThis pattern allows us to store the mapping per restriction instead of per-level. We can then \"enrich\" this in the policyEngine with parameters and subqueries at each level.\n\nThis provides us with an object which we can build any way wee like to get SQL back for a given restriction\n\n* feat: Add ability to fetch subqueries for multiple restrictions at once\n\n* feat(AcquisitionsClient): Added ability to fetch all protected pairs in single fetch\n\n* refactor: Swap over to fetching restrictive AND non-restrictive units for a restriction in a single fetch\n\nStill todo -- multi-restriction fetch amalgamation\n\n* refactor: AcquisitionsClient can now handle fetching user acquisition units for multiple different restrictions at once only making 2 calls instead of 3*number_of_restrictions\n\nPerformance seems kinda bad still, but I think that Sunflower is chugging... remains to be seen on snapshot\n\n* refactor: Tweak the provider pattern to instead pass an ERTParameterProvider implementation\n\nStill not happy with this at the moment, but this will allow me to move onto CREATE\n\n* refactor: GrailsERTParameterProvider\n\nAdded Grails implementation of the ERTParameterProvider interface which we can build with a policyControlledManager, resourceId and startLevel, so that it can be built per request and we don''t have to pass all of that information into the PolicyEngine\n\n* feat: CREATE is now mapped from the owner in the request body\n\n* refactor: Some code moving and documentation writing\n\n* feat: CLAIM now works at any level in the ownership tree\n\n* feat: Policies fetch now returns mapped list of all policies for all ownership levels\n\nNeeds refactors\n\n* refactor: Minor refactors... more needed\n\n* feat: Delete now also handles any AccessPolicyEntity objects for the deleted resource\n\nAlso refactored and renamed a bunch of stuff\n\n* docs: Javadocs\n\n* docs: Javadoc comments\n\n* test: Add test for AcquisitionUnitPolicyEngine\n\n* feat: Make use of new PolicyControlled features for entitlement control\n\n* fix: Re-allow orphaned owner CREATE of Entitlements. This may need revisiting though -- see comments\n\n* fix(AcquisitionUnitPolicySubquery): SQL should return 1=1 for TRUE not just 1\n\n* fix: Allow for empty subqueries","tree":{"sha":"3c1d009e115d5c6d9504f82c11587597c68b15b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/mod-agreements/git/trees/3c1d009e115d5c6d9504f82c11587597c68b15b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/mod-agreements/git/commits/1964947df0264ca88010c939bfbf0b5ae46ce1e2","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c1d009e115d5c6d9504f82c11587597c68b15b8\nparent 0e87249c4ba4cfacd80937f1442df4193b8dc087\nauthor EthanFreestone <54310740+EthanFreestone@users.noreply.github.com> 1764945311 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1764945311 +0000\n\nfeat: Resource access policies do not protect agreement line creation -- ERM-3862 (#957)\n\n* feat: PolicyControlled Restriction owner mappings\n\nAdded a mapping from each level of the ownership chain in PolicyControlledManager, corresponding to how that level handles a given restriction\n\n(options include pass through to owner, use standalone policies, both, or neither)\n\nAdded test assertion to that effect in PolicyControlledManagerTest\n\n* fix: Undo accidental TODO change, not necessary\n\n* fix: Javadoc failed\n\n* feat(PolicyControlledManager): Add helper functions for getting a particular owner level safely and returning the size of the ownership chain\n\n* feat(RestrictionMapEntry): Enhance builder with fluent accessors and maintain equality/hashcode\n\n* feat(PolicyControlledValidator): Set up Validator class to validate uses of @PolicyControlled\n\nNewly mandatory: resourceIdColumn, resourceIdField and resourceTableName\n\nTest updates to match\n\n* feat(PolicyControlledManager): Ability for PolicyControlledManager to spit out SQL for obtaining a given owner level''s id\n\n* docs(PolicyControlledManager): javadoc extension\n\n* feat(AccessPolicyAwareController): !WIP! Set up ownership chain parsing for getPolicySql\n\n* fix(session): Fix session management to marry up to changes on master\n\n* refactor: Start ownership level at 0 instead of -1 for the policyControlledManager ownership chain\n\nI _think_ this is no longer needed thanks to the SQL creation built into the policyControlledManager\n\n* fix: Previous changes had broken the CLAIM operation\n\nThis does NOT introduce the changes required to have standalone CLAIM policies on every level, only to fix what had been previously broken\n\n* chore: Include a clause label in the SQL generated by AcquisitionUnitPolicySubquery\n\nALSO... note that this is creating SQL via DIRECT string SQL injection. It must be INCREDIBLY careful to only set these parameters via trusted code.\n\nUnfortunately this is somewhat unavoidable when trying to set up dynamic SQL. Attempt to mitigate by avoiding any dodgy SQL characters (hopefully)\n\n* fix: More SQL injection protection -- now allows for hibernate style {alias} as well\n\n* fix: More SQL injection protection -- now allows for hibernate style {alias} as well\n\n* feat: Swap the building of SQL up the hierarchy over to an object oriented methodology\n\n* refactor: Move the bulk of the RestrictionTree creation logic and subquery fetching logic at each level over to core components\n\n* refactor: Set up RestrictionTree skeleton which lives on the PolicyControlledManager\n\nThis pattern allows us to store the mapping per restriction instead of per-level. We can then \"enrich\" this in the policyEngine with parameters and subqueries at each level.\n\nThis provides us with an object which we can build any way wee like to get SQL back for a given restriction\n\n* feat: Add ability to fetch subqueries for multiple restrictions at once\n\n* feat(AcquisitionsClient): Added ability to fetch all protected pairs in single fetch\n\n* refactor: Swap over to fetching restrictive AND non-restrictive units for a restriction in a single fetch\n\nStill todo -- multi-restriction fetch amalgamation\n\n* refactor: AcquisitionsClient can now handle fetching user acquisition units for multiple different restrictions at once only making 2 calls instead of 3*number_of_restrictions\n\nPerformance seems kinda bad still, but I think that Sunflower is chugging... remains to be seen on snapshot\n\n* refactor: Tweak the provider pattern to instead pass an ERTParameterProvider implementation\n\nStill not happy with this at the moment, but this will allow me to move onto CREATE\n\n* refactor: GrailsERTParameterProvider\n\nAdded Grails implementation of the ERTParameterProvider interface which we can build with a policyControlledManager, resourceId and startLevel, so that it can be built per request and we don''t have to pass all of that information into the PolicyEngine\n\n* feat: CREATE is now mapped from the owner in the request body\n\n* refactor: Some code moving and documentation writing\n\n* feat: CLAIM now works at any level in the ownership tree\n\n* feat: Policies fetch now returns mapped list of all policies for all ownership levels\n\nNeeds refactors\n\n* refactor: Minor refactors... more needed\n\n* feat: Delete now also handles any AccessPolicyEntity objects for the deleted resource\n\nAlso refactored and renamed a bunch of stuff\n\n* docs: Javadocs\n\n* docs: Javadoc comments\n\n* test: Add test for AcquisitionUnitPolicyEngine\n\n* feat: Make use of new PolicyControlled features for entitlement control\n\n* fix: Re-allow orphaned owner CREATE of Entitlements. This may need revisiting though -- see comments\n\n* fix(AcquisitionUnitPolicySubquery): SQL should return 1=1 for TRUE not just 1\n\n* fix: Allow for empty subqueries","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpMu2fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIp4QADGqWxhPtiQiZYv+z6ijNCjQ\n4izSqEKabAaKdbbXx7Q7uMmSzbIiwZwegZnlEKJr9wsRQkP9v6X93LE25fwu6ly3\nC7XuFtu7FKWT6UJBKgbXlCNuScPbGlT+jo/uUDXmDJmL+yTB53e+8TlpiKfOkAJM\nmuauxcAzw/wOb8epF8GzKIs2uPPWBxNmcptB0kiNMjgrSmHSeiMequNDaGCnd017\nsPirE85eEjfNBex+Mbuyq3Pst6m+5rvBVv7TgFXVOCeb+dJHU0NyDEIojkvt5CVd\nxznYBLdLnILdT+tWxZs7ZVIcmnmGsFff8cVL+OIVPhpmi9yj7po6UFFI0CTIT8Gi\nQuPMjQtlsQQMWjziBIqdZHGHFE4mBETY0nyu68rGK3W1ejpbKv7xgX6aFjXcyIZ0\n8tPYjbOaado+D/T+OSTfkUTve/qO/nGTILEM2ipM7J/4/YiZzxRQrUOPGfLDZahI\nO1OA31TAZYs9uT39adHwaxh094IxCOK3nLFKfsgxmudIqYfQZXvu0sQa+1eCJtCv\n/v5GGdypdw1DmeE0qw6KYfLrhA9YblAJH7Ounb8sMqFyxZyGxqwBV2g8meU7