e-brandon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjQ3NzUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/insights-chrome/commits/c42f29aac0c5e12c88d2519984872c8b6a7904ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T19:42:22Z","email":"btweed@redhat.com","name":"Brandon Tweed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T19:42:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Add platform infrastructure tests for Akamai redirects and route reachability (RHCLOUD-47546) (#3650)\n\n* feat: Add platform infrastructure tests for Akamai redirects and route reachability\n\nPlaywright-based infrastructure validation tests that run via Konflux\nCronJob on a scheduled basis. Uses APIRequestContext (no browser) to\ntest HTTP redirect behavior and route availability against stage/prod.\n\n- Akamai redirect tests: 26 route pairs migrated from iqe-platform-ui\n- Route reachability tests: 13 key application routes verified for 200 OK\n- Environment-parameterized (stage/prod) with squid proxy support for stage\n- Serial execution with 250ms rate limiting to avoid Akamai WAF\n- global-setup guards for auth-less runs (redirect tests need no SSO)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Replace smoke test with Playwright platform infra tests\n\nUpdate the pipeline to clone the repo, install Playwright, and run\nthe Akamai redirect and route reachability tests against prod.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Exclude platform-infra tests from default Playwright runs\n\nThese tests are scheduled independently via Konflux CronJob and should\nnot run as part of regular PR checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Skip squid proxy in CI environments\n\nThe Konflux cluster can reach console.stage.redhat.com directly. The\nsquid proxy is only needed when running tests locally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Exit with test status code after writing results\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Make testIgnore conditional so scheduled pipeline can discover tests\n\nThe PLATFORM_INFRA_ENV env var is set by the pipeline, which lifts the\nignore pattern for scheduled runs while keeping it active for PR checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Update redirect routes from Akamai policy er_console v55\n\nAdds 17 missing redirects, removes 6 stale self-redirect entries, and\ndeduplicates stage/prod route arrays since the Akamai policy applies\nidentically to both environments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Add OpenShift Google Cloud cross-host redirect tests\n\nTests the 6 redirect rules from openshift.googlecloud.redhat.com to\nconsole.redhat.com, covering overview, OSD, OCP, and cluster list paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Sort imports and fix line length for linter\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"780645cb4a4a7e561db661abe3b3f8a7551b08b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/insights-chrome/git/trees/780645cb4a4a7e561db661abe3b3f8a7551b08b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/insights-chrome/git/commits/c42f29aac0c5e12c88d2519984872c8b6a7904ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 780645cb4a4a7e561db661abe3b3f8a7551b08b2\nparent 6c557024cc1abe89b94a933c570a3aaa0231552f\nauthor Brandon Tweed <btweed@redhat.com> 1788378142 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788378142 +0200\n\nfeat: Add platform infrastructure tests for Akamai redirects and route reachability (RHCLOUD-47546) (#3650)\n\n* feat: Add platform infrastructure tests for Akamai redirects and route reachability\n\nPlaywright-based infrastructure validation tests that run via Konflux\nCronJob on a scheduled basis. Uses APIRequestContext (no browser) to\ntest HTTP redirect behavior and route availability against stage/prod.\n\n- Akamai redirect tests: 26 route pairs migrated from iqe-platform-ui\n- Route reachability tests: 13 key application routes verified for 200 OK\n- Environment-parameterized (stage/prod) with squid proxy support for stage\n- Serial execution with 250ms rate limiting to avoid Akamai WAF\n- global-setup guards for auth-less runs (redirect tests need no SSO)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Replace smoke test with Playwright platform infra tests\n\nUpdate the pipeline to clone the repo, install Playwright, and run\nthe Akamai redirect and route reachability tests against prod.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Exclude platform-infra tests from default Playwright runs\n\nThese tests are scheduled independently via Konflux CronJob and should\nnot run as part of regular PR checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Skip squid proxy in CI environments\n\nThe Konflux cluster can reach console.stage.redhat.com directly. The\nsquid proxy is only needed when running tests locally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Exit with test status code after writing results\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Make testIgnore conditional so scheduled pipeline can discover tests\n\nThe PLATFORM_INFRA_ENV env var is set by the pipeline, which lifts the\nignore pattern for scheduled runs while keeping it active for PR checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Update redirect routes from Akamai policy er_console v55\n\nAdds 17 missing redirects, removes 6 stale self-redirect entries, and\ndeduplicates stage/prod route arrays since the Akamai policy applies\nidentically to both environments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Add OpenShift Google Cloud cross-host redirect tests\n\nTests the 6 redirect rules from openshift.googlecloud.redhat.com to\nconsole.redhat.com, covering overview, OSD, OCP, and cluster list paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Sort imports and fix line length for linter\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmHweCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADi0QAGVdjoCSrJqZCS4cwHdOMZ81\nA4TL7krchoOzQSOAMy9pnmXhONjeqDXvLTsPMjxCZw+T0LTEqJZGE3itiC3bYOmy\nX9IN4kfxtTrw7ynDkv4FD7tETYK8POY+ilPcz3EjLECIpeEYDAfMMNg6muJVnjvO\nogrF9o+A4e3g9ZgeQdIxzY/osTi8tnbLuYcef0NtL7GZwW89cj7kC7L6KnByVn5J\nROred94zqej9twEl51HQfI0PVNbKJ25gDE+VTLAwtrm+va9cIEbTbEGZMGcm4VRw\nUdustzKdph34DwpE1rRgufwC+Vr/i1jrWfeUjJr96ssCu1AdwDRv3EM/tkMNRXk0\niWCdOE7Iqfr/v7me7AYnkVsvSB2Uq+PDr8zg6QhbYSslcq8tZwDf/l7AycORkBy9\nzHJyYrKAt42FUlsQw6W2UG4mdyK+KfLGoTRtKoXzI1UsF8BbbjsH6FqAMvze84/W\nVVyl7CQqbq5bgmJdGkybsG6MpUMmG2XXYX36I4L8pl4tFWidmYexe3yEs8Rz6RV8\ngGFgMnh3G3BSIetYJgD/Y1Kl1ed+d8PUTmiLD8kJNGwfWPhbwiJVoWE/KTqxzmb1\naf84tWfuURN+ojH4PQNkRjlzJIm4hHudZwWLaJM9HDoXt7f5RK0CRwzV9/q2+YKr\n0xjgkbGxlCUWfMrDI8fY\n=ifvw\n-----