,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxpyDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvUMQAH0HTXc6Zi8aESyi4KmFD8Si\nfFzbQu+uXW95mbd0JR0u7vR/q8DeZJuYaT+XACB8SOCpN7xicp/petABXqK1Cz+b\nOQlCZbSI+TG7Z1SpfS/ZBoDye+iKe083PNG+p76IaCIogw6nZuZ99ZeDBOCh50TB\npo59di/RyV+b6dgcWwQCcKOIL+POzDaobT7SbZEe7PstvfOKPwDK2X4REwS1XlGj\nkqnGND5dfaH8syfde9ZVPni66WKkYsT7P0+gY6zvswTbKSeBmLZXq/8U1C0N6To9\nMCDbHiRQBVkAgSxC26LgXO0Pou9jgKGGCZG1cFCzIYgfS045tNioREPPE6yVp2BD\nAlqlWNYCABh7RFcNhfbiMhE1HeFBplSNH2t/MatmnvGo4bTJ5dCOKsLZ+8Mq8j8h\nehbI5jYkHbpjDmfeRoMGtlps4KfrnAWql7TcxHrnzzutxQ8sOTj+UjkOYIHnfZrS\nsWbKJ5+g7NgFG3XxqT6fCxTtxE8eqtjvFOlpfVoR5wFDlf2ryPNtEXdTR0MyDRW8\nd5Z5r0Eqm95EEK8q4R7vM4qMHrULZmuQROQ0/SInAGn/v9l6e9tGlJvcEA9ymgNW\nEOCgu5IZMVo9t8pVL90QXVENOGbBw5wRSD+9wTW2qrxrLQ801WBlUfHgYjOo1LQt\n+C72QaRlHyDmRn9yep+H\n=32tm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T19:24:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/6491df0bec6e062dfe276ae7da31e75b42021161","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKDY0OTFkZjBiZWM2ZTA2MmRmZTI3NmFlN2RhMzFlNzViNDIwMjExNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/4ae5c0f05776ba4ddd576ddbd07db849e9387d55","sha":"4ae5c0f05776ba4ddd576ddbd07db849e9387d55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/4ae5c0f05776ba4ddd576ddbd07db849e9387d55"}],"sha":"6491df0bec6e062dfe276ae7da31e75b42021161","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/6491df0bec6e062dfe276ae7da31e75b42021161"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58434978?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jsinovassin","id":58434978,"login":"jsinovassin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NDM0OTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsinovassin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/4ae5c0f05776ba4ddd576ddbd07db849e9387d55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:12:38Z","email":"58434978+jsinovassin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jonathan SINOVASSIN-NAIK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:12:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: stop page saves from reordering sub-pages the editor did not move (#2800)\n\n* fix: stop page saves from reordering sub-pages the editor did not move\n\n* test: use breakAclInheritance from @jahia/cypress\n\n* refactor: look up the ordered names in a set\n\n* feat: lock the sub-pages that the editor cannot move, and count the hidden ones\n\nThe ordering list of the edit form shows a lock on a child that the user cannot move. A new mutation field, reorderMovableChildren, keeps each such child in its position when the other children move. Jackrabbit refuses to reorder a child without jcr:removeNode on it, so reorderChildren failed on such a child.\n\nA new field, hiddenChildrenCount, counts the children that the user cannot read. When the count is above 0, the list shows the count and does not allow a reorder, because a move cannot keep a hidden child in its position.\n\nThe permission tests log in as the editor in each test. The cy.apollo command authenticates as root in the browser session, so a stored editor session came back as root.\n\nSurefire ignores the TestNG version of the parent, so the new JUnit test runs.\n\n* test: read the sub-page order with getNodeByPath\n\n* fix: check the privileges that Jackrabbit needs to reorder a child\n\nJackrabbit checks MODIFY_CHILD_NODE_COLLECTION on the moved child, and Jahia maps it to jcr:addChildNodes and jcr:removeChildNodes. The lock used jcr:removeNode, which matched these two privileges only for the standard roles.\n\nThe ordering logic moves to ChildrenOrderingUtils, and the GraphQL extensions call it. The edit form reads the new canBeReordered field, so the rule is in one place.\n\n* chore: drop the license header from the new files, and pin the surefire version\n\n* fix: refuse a reorder while a child is hidden, and count the hidden children once\n\nreorderMovableChildren could not keep the position of a child that the user cannot read, so a direct GraphQL call still moved it. The mutation now fails when the parent has such a child.\n\nhiddenChildrenCount takes no argument and counts every hidden child, so the edit form blocks the reorder exactly when the mutation would refuse it. The form asks for one count instead of two.\n\n* fix: keep reorderChildren for the page builder, and use reorderMovableChildren for the edit form only\n\nThe page builder creates and pastes at an insertion point through SavePropertiesMutation, with childrenOrder set to the new node and the node it goes before. reorderMovableChildren refills the positions that the names hold, so the new node took the place of the next sibling, and that sibling went to the end.\n\nThe mutation takes reorderChildren again with shouldModifyChildren and childrenOrder, as on main, and the onEdit hooks keep that contract. The edit form sends its order in shouldReorderMovableChildren and movableChildrenOrder.\n\n* fix: match hidden children by identifier and count the listed types only\n\n* fix: disable the moves that cross a locked child, and keep the list when every child is hidden\n\n* refactor: read the listed node types from the Jahia constants\n\n* test: check the locked ends of the list on a page of its own","tree":{"sha":"5622fa1351e0a44f7a43d411ac49bc896841cd5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/5622fa1351e0a44f7a43d411ac49bc896841cd5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/4ae5c0f05776ba4ddd576ddbd07db849e9387d55","verification":{"payload":"tree 5622fa1351e0a44f7a43d411ac49bc896841cd5d\nparent 0b14d845739c6ffb74a957976a6460f5ce06adc4\nauthor Jonathan SINOVASSIN-NAIK <58434978+jsinovassin@users.noreply.github.com> 1791393158 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791393158 -0400\n\nfix: stop page saves from reordering sub-pages the editor did not move (#2800)\n\n* fix: stop page saves from reordering sub-pages the editor did not move\n\n* test: use breakAclInheritance from @jahia/cypress\n\n* refactor: look up the ordered names in a set\n\n* feat: lock the sub-pages that the editor cannot move, and count the hidden ones\n\nThe ordering list of the edit form shows a lock on a child that the user cannot move. A new mutation field, reorderMovableChildren, keeps each such child in its position when the other children move. Jackrabbit refuses to reorder a child without jcr:removeNode on it, so reorderChildren failed on such a child.\n\nA new field, hiddenChildrenCount, counts the children that the user cannot read. When the count is above 0, the list shows the count and does not allow a reorder, because a move cannot keep a hidden child in its position.\n\nThe permission tests log in as the editor in each test. The cy.apollo command authenticates as root in the browser session, so a stored editor session came back as root.\n\nSurefire ignores the TestNG version of the parent, so the new JUnit test runs.\n\n* test: read the sub-page order with getNodeByPath\n\n* fix: check the privileges that Jackrabbit needs to reorder a child\n\nJackrabbit checks MODIFY_CHILD_NODE_COLLECTION on the moved child, and Jahia maps it to jcr:addChildNodes and jcr:removeChildNodes. The lock used jcr:removeNode, which matched these two privileges only for the standard roles.\n\nThe ordering logic moves to ChildrenOrderingUtils, and the GraphQL extensions call it. The edit form reads the new canBeReordered field, so the rule is in one place.\n\n* chore: drop the license header from the new files, and pin the surefire version\n\n* fix: refuse a reorder while a child is hidden, and count the hidden children once\n\nreorderMovableChildren could not keep the position of a child that the user cannot read, so a direct GraphQL call still moved it. The mutation now fails when the parent has such a child.\n\nhiddenChildrenCount takes no argument and counts every hidden child, so the edit form blocks the reorder exactly when the mutation would refuse it. The form asks for one count instead of two.\n\n* fix: keep reorderChildren for the page builder, and use reorderMovableChildren for the edit form only\n\nThe page builder creates and pastes at an insertion point through SavePropertiesMutation, with childrenOrder set to the new node and the node it goes before. reorderMovableChildren refills the positions that the names hold, so the new node took the place of the next sibling, and that sibling went to the end.\n\nThe mutation takes reorderChildren again with shouldModifyChildren and childrenOrder, as on main, and the onEdit hooks keep that contract. The edit form sends its order in shouldReorderMovableChildren and movableChildrenOrder.\n\n* fix: match hidden children by identifier and count the listed types only\n\n* fix: disable the moves that cross a locked child, and keep the list when every child is hidden\n\n* refactor: read the listed node types from the Jahia constants\n\n* test: check the locked ends of the list on a page of its own","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxn2GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAklMQAGDq+sROubmvsV2Ahve9uTTk\nfQhl0yPg5EgK9ia+kYER0Pkti+odYKG0vYyLhT/OBV57s7+qTKMA8jO9DUMSAlNa\ncFnI2POeWaNzmVUB24s33J5NiL/wICqt6HjRV7IwmRGiQuE0OK9p86Wx4z4Se2wx\nIpaqDVKDB64CjP7BhLQr1TkUmHjgUoPH65pZy8gnYQdSyzcRnSvFGDp3U2tagKt1\nX5WmuuGD+QqPUKxq89iWaf5i/Xq+XT7B15EZbctSwugXWpzHJgcSM/p6YgN47wVt\nWwOmK6lFjlP48JJI0I0W89QoPkVjFaXmzFWNO+fzvEMyiuMkfdWbMbqfHE5o0P5o\n4yyvgDWtn/44waIMhjkga/8ZkdHzbaSy+Xk1kTuZOXNQfqkdg0t/Hg2ok5HAmejT\n0fSmxaboirJ5awCU4s6wx1XgX7O6GSlDfcvLlFxy0QTWCZRdhHn0t7zUXJP1YGfh\nPvA0k0DyweQWSH7OySzah9HK9rYyKE6G/kQnNYW89YW1Rwi33S5xCBmkcE1GvyiA\n3BRKnl26crpqYwC6Bb38f7GnPw+1iCa92cjWmddgJ7+cYbzrtVX8GdlCl3Nh4KGP\n38AvouS7aBJh7WcHusa1EUZMV3iIjdoCnSnlz28ktUTUhxt/5miX8t1rb9QEcTCS\n6313UaO/R+WyjhAgm6/a\n=1pM7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T17:12:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url"