19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/7c57f41fd683f93f2779b505c398e5a6511694dc","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKDdjNTdmNDFmZDY4M2Y5M2YyNzc5YjUwNWMzOThlNWE2NTExNjk0ZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/1bcd94763f7aac84fe76a0d57b2e2646da8e1db2","sha":"1bcd94763f7aac84fe76a0d57b2e2646da8e1db2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/1bcd94763f7aac84fe76a0d57b2e2646da8e1db2"}],"sha":"7c57f41fd683f93f2779b505c398e5a6511694dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/7c57f41fd683f93f2779b505c398e5a6511694dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80773810?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheKlem","id":80773810,"login":"TheKlem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNzczODEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/1bcd94763f7aac84fe76a0d57b2e2646da8e1db2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:41:52Z","email":"80773810+TheKlem@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TheKlem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:41:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: close dialogs when the page behind them changes (#2727)\n\nDialogs opened through the component renderer are mounted next to the router\nrather than inside it, so a route change unmounts nothing: the dialog stays on\nscreen on top of the page the user has just navigated to. It is most visible\nwith the browser''s back button, which leaves the mark for deletion dialog\nfloating over the previous page.\n\nuseCloseOnNavigation closes the dialog once the application has navigated, the\nway its cancel button would, so the graceful close each dialog already\nimplements still runs and the renderer entry is destroyed. The location is read\nfrom the store rather than from the router hooks precisely because of where\nthose dialogs are mounted: the router context is not guaranteed to reach them,\nwhile the store provider wraps the whole application - the delete dialog\nalready relies on that.\n\nWatching the pathname alone is not enough, and would have missed the very case\nreported: jContent records the selected node in the query string, so opening a\ndialog from a selected item and going back moves between two entries sharing a\npathname. The browser buttons are recognized by the POP action the store keeps\nnext to the location instead, which holds whatever part of the url changed. A\npush or a replace keeping the same pathname stays ignored, since that is how\nthe current page records its own state - a selection in jContent, an open\neditor in the Content Editor hash - rather than a page change.\n\nApplied to the dialogs that are only a decision to take: delete, undelete,\nexport, work in progress, create folder, rename, download, usages, customized\npreview and the save error modal. The upload panel and the zip/unzip progress\noverlay are deliberately left alone, since the work they report on carries on\nwhile the user browses, as is the image editor, which would silently discard\npending edits.\n\nFixes #2089","tree":{"sha":"d21171143782b711468adab1d61fb3cbddb0eb1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/d21171143782b711468adab1d61fb3cbddb0eb1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/1bcd94763f7aac84fe76a0d57b2e2646da8e1db2","verification":{"payload":"tree d21171143782b711468adab1d61fb3cbddb0eb1f\nparent 745a846d49461ed4b511c66476d0fea55b50081a\nauthor TheKlem <80773810+TheKlem@users.noreply.github.com> 1790768512 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790768512 +0200\n\nfix: close dialogs when the page behind them changes (#2727)\n\nDialogs opened through the component renderer are mounted next to the router\nrather than inside it, so a route change unmounts nothing: the dialog stays on\nscreen on top of the page the user has just navigated to. It is most visible\nwith the browser''s back button, which leaves the mark for deletion dialog\nfloating over the previous page.\n\nuseCloseOnNavigation closes the dialog once the application has navigated, the\nway its cancel button would, so the graceful close each dialog already\nimplements still runs and the renderer entry is destroyed. The location is read\nfrom the store rather than from the router hooks precisely because of where\nthose dialogs are mounted: the router context is not guaranteed to reach them,\nwhile the store provider wraps the whole application - the delete dialog\nalready relies on that.\n\nWatching the pathname alone is not enough, and would have missed the very case\nreported: jContent records the selected node in the query string, so opening a\ndialog from a selected item and going back moves between two entries sharing a\npathname. The browser buttons are recognized by the POP action the store keeps\nnext to the location instead, which holds whatever part of the url changed. A\npush or a replace keeping the same pathname stays ignored, since that is how\nthe current page records its own state - a selection in jContent, an open\neditor in the Content Editor hash - rather than a page change.\n\nApplied to the dialogs that are only a decision to take: delete, undelete,\nexport, work in progress, create folder, rename, download, usages, customized\npreview and the save error modal. The upload panel and the zip/unzip progress\noverlay are deliberately left alone, since the work they report on carries on\nwhile the user browses, as is the image editor, which would silently discard\npending edits.\n\nFixes #2089","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPWACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAId0QAE+jo/L2XLgM3vDAqbQpbBdx\nnn5bz9VhzZeVa71Qkz5g3k5p2eDJ2lYvAtLk+g6j8yf4pv+v4u53+phzAYFpILJv\nE2ghSUzaPEvLgO4tGhGv6nz02v7gaYYoIx4RR1rXH9y9RKyk43yYkCVVDqi6ov2z\ndRs9FzBdRYGWZWzII9etT3GDWX77GufJlykCfAyrw8SMWmTZU7YkewxMldnP/7qm\nsDBBSh9il2pszzpXL5ZWDn/WwU/LmH7bW2HtNPbhuZ/2sChBiezvUubql7j932GX\ngBbZYoC+p0mplhs8zbRucXcI+2EUnhxnmAUKEwoKQ75uTFeJGBlRjDEqCdwLTj1S\n6vHGxTP8zX13Vq0s3rV8TiPitrcmNo7dYmvfT70uQ+dKg/EzUm9B5GyTy+XgmIrs\nIehLJJk2Y4Roonec5AJUvM+483M/Ufrl3TLuJsOSUbAZrDnXNf7oavB/d5E4jBS6\nPnGfmorBM35DKAcnNePhy52IcM+bwbVA6s18AMbhcXEWJ1LNGdw+hdzE5fh0Crej\nKkM1ZJ/CEWD4nrNArwoo/MdnuOTTT8qCy3LCOinsu8dqw9MnY88wz29ZpAFVoXzZ\nWZuFbSUUNos8C3aXSMWebHEejXvKBGy4ZJVdmdsTQRG6or4ygdeRIPz5VX/f9JaY\nuL7mCUkSMMCyXlki0lBO\n=A7Vj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:41:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/1bcd94763f7aac84fe76a0d57b2e2646da8e1db2","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKDFiY2Q5NDc2M2Y3YWFjODRmZTc2YTBkNTdiMmUyNjQ2ZGE4ZTFkYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/745a846d49461ed4b511c66476d0fea55b50081a","sha":"745a846d49461ed4b511c66476d0fea55b50081a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/745a846d49461ed4b511c66476d0fea55b50081a"}],"sha":"1bcd94763f7aac84fe76a0d57b2e2646da8e1db2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/1bcd94763f7aac84fe76a0d57b2e2646da8e1db2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80773810?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheKlem","id":80773810,"login":"TheKlem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNzczODEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/745a846d49461ed4b511c66476d0fea55b50081a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:02:54Z","email":"80773810+TheKlem@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TheKlem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:02:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: keep the page reachable in the breadcrumbs from a node under it (#2729)\n\n* fix: keep the page reachable in the breadcrumbs from a node under it\n\nBrowsing into a node the content tree does not show - an area, typically -\ncollapsed the whole breadcrumb to the single page the node sits under, and the\nrule that greys out the last entry then greyed out that page: it was the only\nthing left on screen and there was no way back to it.\n\ngetItems has a branch for the case where the closest ancestor visible in the\ncontent tree is the direct parent, and it returns that ancestor alone. It was\nwritten when no branch appended the node itself, so returning just the parent\nwas consistent with the rest. \"Add self to breadcrumb path\" (#1309) later added\nthe node to the three other returns and missed this one, and \"Disable\nbreadcrumbs\" (#1312) turned what was left into a dead end.\n\nThe branch is not needed: with the parent as the last visible ancestor, the\ngeneral path below it slices an empty list of remaining ancestors and returns\nexactly the same two entries, the parent and the node. Removing it restores the\npage as a navigable entry, with the node itself as the current one.\n\nFixes #1908\n\n* test: cover the breadcrumb from a node the content tree does not show\n\nThe reviewer asked for the fix to be covered in the jcontent breadcrumbs\ncypress suite, not only in the unit test.\n\narea-main is a jnt:contentList under subpageA, which is itself two levels\nbelow the site root - the shape that used to collapse the breadcrumb to\nthe parent page alone and grey it out. The test asserts the page entry is\npresent and enabled, the area is the current (disabled) one, and clicking\nthe page navigates back to it.\n\n* test: capitalize the comment to satisfy eslint capitalized-comments\n\n* test: assert the breadcrumb entries on the buttons, not their labels\n\nBreadcrumb.findByContent goes through cy.contains, which yields the deepest\nelement holding the text - the moonstone label span inside the button. A span\nhas no disabled state, so ''be.disabled'' could never hold on the current entry,\nand ''not.be.disabled'' on the parent page held for the wrong reason: the check\nthat was meant to guard the regression passed whatever the entry did.\n\nThe assertions now run against the buttons inside the breadcrumb nav, and state\nthe shape the fix produces: two entries, the page first and enabled, the area\nsecond and disabled.","tree":{"sha":"621a203395e64025c839a754b71cf5a27243fd9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/621a203395e64025c839a754b71cf5a27243fd9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/745a846d49461ed4b511c66476d0fea55b50081a","verification":{"payload":"tree 621a203395e64025c839a754b71cf5a27243fd9b\nparent 1ba4bc09d6832ffc2e4db67a4206276c89b036c1\nauthor TheKlem <80773810+TheKlem@users.noreply.github.com> 1790686974 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790686974 +0200\n\nfix: keep the page reachable in the breadcrumbs from a node under it (#2729)\n\n* fix: keep the page reachable in the breadcrumbs from a node under it\n\nBrowsing into a node the content tree does not show - an area, typically -\ncollapsed the whole breadcrumb to the single page the node sits under, and the\nrule that greys out the last entry then greyed out that page: it was the only\nthing left on screen and there was no way back to it.\n\ngetItems has a branch for the case where the closest ancestor visible in the\ncontent tree is the direct parent, and it returns that ancestor alone. It was\nwritten when no branch appended the node itself, so returning just the parent\nwas consistent with the rest. \"Add self to breadcrumb path\" (#1309) later added\nthe node to the three other returns and missed this one, and \"Disable\nbreadcrumbs\" (#1312) turned what was left into a dead end.\n\nThe branch is not needed: with the parent as the last visible ancestor, the\ngeneral path below it slices an empty list of remaining ancestors and returns\nexactly the same two entries, the parent and the node. Removing it restores the\npage as a navigable entry, with the node itself as the current one.\n\nFixes #1908\n\n* test: cover the breadcrumb from a node the content tree does not show\n\nThe reviewer asked for the fix to be covered in the jcontent breadcrumbs\ncypress suite, not only in the unit test.\n\narea-main is a jnt:contentList under subpageA, which is itself two levels\nbelow the site root - the shape that used to collapse the breadcrumb to\nthe parent page alone and grey it out. The test asserts the page entry is\npresent and enabled, the area is the current (disabled) one, and clicking\nthe page navigates back to it.\n\n* test: capitalize the comment to satisfy eslint capitalized-comments\n\n* test: assert the breadcrumb entries on the buttons, not their labels\n\nBreadcrumb.findByContent goes through cy.contains, which yields the deepest\nelement holding the text - the moonstone label span inside the button. A span\nhas no disabled state, so ''be.disabled'' could never hold on the current entry,\nand ''not.be.disabled'' on the parent page held for the wrong reason: the check\nthat was meant to guard the regression passed whatever the entry did.\n\nThe assertions now run against the buttons inside the breadcrumb nav, and state\nthe shape the fix produces: two entries, the page first and enabled, the area\nsecond and disabled.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu7b+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJFkQAIneoIMtvhrczPcxY95vGbae\nc+ttpIaT6HRpDe55ilWOqzMoklSDmu/hiossWZ045jwHZ3+C66QMwg/E3mVIyZEF\nnW5V85PtNeKm0EmGYSV2fawrTue1Rcsrooj69emgZp2yzU3xYgZJ4AeciEdGP06f\nMVDtPxjD3mWaJtmbtcxPatlZgPoi9EOZtJIGtw1rRjk0hQ6XcMnn+YwDR7Lakbrk\ngH7b3F1DB+TXBj2CD2KVxr06xfsDl62sj5lLzb2A67LFywQZ5Of5r2k4fUtLHSiK\nqry8zJ5vc/S3aDM4kPwMd1sLLvNjcofyAK4dFXdxswpsABC8VoBP/h1ziLV1ANjh\nifPYX2l91ATaI5lU43eUzlPJq+V+K1w1bSClqaVKQ8INKN6JK0DQ0ChO32EZJaIH\ncCunORdM9bJTgEAg+E7I3vMvjDVEEgb9HNVKAxkQYwXjW1W4X5ekxPvKWK0ncV5d\n9iWPUDnThz3A+rEbEH2tfsSs7tFEizKCsHZlPl1mSwsJtKo/nDxt4HawimmceKtM\neas247YtsyASJGJFhZVBhxAyIXggmrMVWPONOekzzuF0GaTuZ5HhA1CTFZEPC2W+\nCMa1SzQjeH+P33rCHY93kdP1+Sth7RwGJhE4Z9GRy5p3BBUx63y2mQteS8fgrgRp\nF/jiegnLHRYW9jnKSdSv\n=zTRB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T13:02:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/745a846d49461ed4b511c66476d0fea55b50081a","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKDc0NWE4NDZkNDk0NjFlZDRiNTExYzY2NDc2ZDBmZWE1NWI1MDA4MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/1ba4bc09d6832ffc2e4db67a4206276c89b036c1","sha":"1ba4bc09d6832ffc2e4db67a4206276c89b036c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/1ba4bc09d6832ffc2e4db67a4206276c89b036c1"}],"sha":"745a846d49461ed4b511c66476d0fea55b50081a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/745a846d49461ed4b511c66476d0fea55b50081a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/1ba4bc09d6832ffc2e4db67a4206276c89b036c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:41:42Z","email":"smonier@Jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:41:4