P SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T17:41:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/1ba4bc09d6832ffc2e4db67a4206276c89b036c1","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKDFiYTRiYzA5ZDY4MzJmZmMyZTRkYjY3YTQyMDYyNzZjODliMDM2YzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/6f743a02bdd9220871ef12906e02e787b762e02f","sha":"6f743a02bdd9220871ef12906e02e787b762e02f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/6f743a02bdd9220871ef12906e02e787b762e02f"}],"sha":"1ba4bc09d6832ffc2e4db67a4206276c89b036c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/1ba4bc09d6832ffc2e4db67a4206276c89b036c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8562956?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AKarmanov","id":8562956,"login":"AKarmanov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NjI5NTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AKarmanov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/6f743a02bdd9220871ef12906e02e787b762e02f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:57:03Z","email":"alexandrk_@hotmail.com","name":"Alex Karmanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:57:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve named child placeholders outside a rendered page (#2780)\n\n* fix: resolve named child placeholders outside a rendered page\n\nNamed child creation actions came only from the capture taken for the\ncurrent route, and that capture exists only where a page is rendered. A\ncontent folder renders no page, so its nodes offered the wildcard type\nalone and every named child was missing.\n\nThe definition cannot stand in for the rendering: a placeholder''s name,\nits node types and whether it appears at all come from the view''s\ntemplate:module tag, from j:contributeTypes and from the node''s\neditability. So render the node itself when the route capture does not\ncover it, through renderedContent in module configuration with edit mode\non, and parse it with the same extractor.\n\nA node rendered on its own carries no module wrapper - the root of an\neditframe render is jahiatype=\"mainmodule\" - so attribute a placeholder\nwith no module ancestor to the rendered node, or every one of them is\ndropped for want of a parent.\n\nAlso fixes three defects in the action that built those entries: the\nnamed actions were pushed onto a memoized array and so appended again on\nevery re-render, the push threw when the creatable types exceeded the\ndirect-button limit, and two named children of one type collided on the\nsame React key.\n\n* fix: keep parentless placeholders out of the page capture\n\nparseModuleInfo attributed a placeholder with no module ancestor to the\nrendered root. A page render reaches that branch too: the page root element\nis a mainmodule, which the module selector never matches, so a placeholder\ndirectly under it was adopted by the page. getNamedPlaceholders then returned\nit for the page path, and the createPage action gained buttons that create\ncontent instead of pages.\n\nThe fallback now applies only when the node was rendered on its own, which is\nthe case it was written for.\n\n* Update src/javascript/ContentEditor/actions/jcontent/createContent/createContentAction.jsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Geofrey Flores <75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update src/javascript/ContentEditor/actions/jcontent/createContent/useNamedChildPlaceholders.js\n\nCo-authored-by: Geofrey Flores <75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: hold the placeholder result steady, and drop one with no type\n\nThe skip flag the create action passes was not read: the hook took only a\npath and a language, so every right-click still rendered the node. It is\nnow forwarded to the query and short-circuits the result.\n\nBoth branches allocated a fresh array on every render, and the rendering\nwas re-parsed each time. That array is a dependency of the action''s memo,\nso the memoization the action relies on was cancelled - the result is now\nmemoized on the inputs that produce it, and the empty case is one shared\narray.\n\nThe rendering omits the nodetypes attribute when neither the view nor the\ndefinition constrains a placeholder, which left the editor with no type to\ncreate. Such a placeholder is dropped, in the one helper both branches now\nshare rather than in a filter each had its own copy of.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Geofrey Flores <75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"aaf83f716e92831f0055a8d6420d575e15f505c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/aaf83f716e92831f0055a8d6420d575e15f505c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/6f743a02bdd9220871ef12906e02e787b762e02f","verification":{"payload":"tree aaf83f716e92831f0055a8d6420d575e15f505c0\nparent b721d8c3804435261000471494e236e85f1252d4\nauthor Alex Karmanov <alexandrk_@hotmail.com> 1789649823 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789649823 -0400\n\nfix: resolve named child placeholders outside a rendered page (#2780)\n\n* fix: resolve named child placeholders outside a rendered page\n\nNamed child creation actions came only from the capture taken for the\ncurrent route, and that capture exists only where a page is rendered. A\ncontent folder renders no page, so its nodes offered the wildcard type\nalone and every named child was missing.\n\nThe definition cannot stand in for the rendering: a placeholder''s name,\nits node types and whether it appears at all come from the view''s\ntemplate:module tag, from j:contributeTypes and from the node''s\neditability. So render the node itself when the route capture does not\ncover it, through renderedContent in module configuration with edit mode\non, and parse it with the same extractor.\n\nA node rendered on its own carries no module wrapper - the root of an\neditframe render is jahiatype=\"mainmodule\" - so attribute a placeholder\nwith no module ancestor to the rendered node, or every one of them is\ndropped for want of a parent.\n\nAlso fixes three defects in the action that built those entries: the\nnamed actions were pushed onto a memoized array and so appended again on\nevery re-render, the push threw when the creatable types exceeded the\ndirect-button limit, and two named children of one type collided on the\nsame React key.\n\n* fix: keep parentless placeholders out of the page capture\n\nparseModuleInfo attributed a placeholder with no module ancestor to the\nrendered root. A page render reaches that branch too: the page root element\nis a mainmodule, which the module selector never matches, so a placeholder\ndirectly under it was adopted by the page. getNamedPlaceholders then returned\nit for the page path, and the createPage action gained buttons that create\ncontent instead of pages.\n\nThe fallback now applies only when the node was rendered on its own, which is\nthe case it was written for.\n\n* Update src/javascript/ContentEditor/actions/jcontent/createContent/createContentAction.jsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Geofrey Flores <75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update src/javascript/ContentEditor/actions/jcontent/createContent/useNamedChildPlaceholders.js\n\nCo-authored-by: Geofrey Flores <75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: hold the placeholder result steady, and drop one with no type\n\nThe skip flag the create action passes was not read: the hook took only a\npath and a language, so every right-click still rendered the node. It is\nnow forwarded to the query and short-circuits the result.\n\nBoth branches allocated a fresh array on every render, and the rendering\nwas re-parsed each time. That array is a dependency of the action''s memo,\nso the memoization the action relies on was cancelled - the result is now\nmemoized on the inputs that produce it, and the empty case is one shared\narray.\n\nThe rendering omits the nodetypes attribute when neither the view nor the\ndefinition constrains a placeholder, which left the editor with no type to\ncreate. Such a placeholder is dropped, in the one helper both branches now\nshare rather than in a filter each had its own copy of.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Geofrey Flores <75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":