id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/b721d8c3804435261000471494e236e85f1252d4","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKGI3MjFkOGMzODA0NDM1MjYxMDAwNDcxNDk0ZTIzNmU4NWYxMjUyZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/a1ac7a147d85157763ef9c43ca9b4738ce507ae8","sha":"a1ac7a147d85157763ef9c43ca9b4738ce507ae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/a1ac7a147d85157763ef9c43ca9b4738ce507ae8"}],"sha":"b721d8c3804435261000471494e236e85f1252d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/b721d8c3804435261000471494e236e85f1252d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42536778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdusolle","id":42536778,"login":"sdusolle","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNTM2Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdusolle","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/a1ac7a147d85157763ef9c43ca9b4738ce507ae8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T15:06:35Z","email":"42536778+sdusolle@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sonia Dusolle"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T15:06:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: update jcontent to 3.7.2-SNAPSHOT (#2777)\n\n* chore: update jcontent to 3.7.2-SNAPSHOT\n\n* chore: carry 3.7.2-SNAPSHOT into the test modules and the snapshot manifest\n\nThe root pom was the only file moved off 3.8.0-SNAPSHOT, so the build\nproduced jcontent-3.7.2-SNAPSHOT.jar next to test artifacts still stamped\n3.8.0-SNAPSHOT. The six files the 3.7.1 bump touched are now in step.\n\nThe snapshot provisioning manifest pinned 3.7.1-SNAPSHOT, which is the\nversion it was left at when the release plugin moved main to 3.8.0. Its\nown comment asks for it to follow the root pom, so it follows it here.\n\n* chore: regenerate the module signature for 3.7.2-SNAPSHOT\n\nkeymaker signs the module identity from the pom, version included, so the\nsignature carried over from 3.8.0-SNAPSHOT no longer matched. Jahia''s\nBundleLicenseCheckerListener answered by uninstalling the bundle, and the\nstart that followed hit an uninstalled revision:\n\n  ERROR [o.j.s.l.BundleLicenseCheckerListener] - Invalid license check\n  Caused by: NullPointerException ... BundleRevision.getWiring() is null\n\nThe CI signing job would not have caught this: it only runs when the last\ncommit message carries [ci sign], and reports success as a no-op otherwise.\nRegenerated with keymaker-cli 2.0, which now reports the pom as valid.","tree":{"sha":"3a9eb72c56addf73bed93af9fccb5d7735825b89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/3a9eb72c56addf73bed93af9fccb5d7735825b89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/a1ac7a147d85157763ef9c43ca9b4738ce507ae8","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a9eb72c56addf73bed93af9fccb5d7735825b89\nparent 73314c1648246bed35950cc5cc2bec8e2bd3ef6c\nauthor Sonia Dusolle <42536778+sdusolle@users.noreply.github.com> 1789484795 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789484795 +0200\n\nchore: update jcontent to 3.7.2-SNAPSHOT (#2777)\n\n* chore: update jcontent to 3.7.2-SNAPSHOT\n\n* chore: carry 3.7.2-SNAPSHOT into the test modules and the snapshot manifest\n\nThe root pom was the only file moved off 3.8.0-SNAPSHOT, so the build\nproduced jcontent-3.7.2-SNAPSHOT.jar next to test artifacts still stamped\n3.8.0-SNAPSHOT. The six files the 3.7.1 bump touched are now in step.\n\nThe snapshot provisioning manifest pinned 3.7.1-SNAPSHOT, which is the\nversion it was left at when the release plugin moved main to 3.8.0. Its\nown comment asks for it to follow the root pom, so it follows it here.\n\n* chore: regenerate the module signature for 3.7.2-SNAPSHOT\n\nkeymaker signs the module identity from the pom, version included, so the\nsignature carried over from 3.8.0-SNAPSHOT no longer matched. Jahia''s\nBundleLicenseCheckerListener answered by uninstalling the bundle, and the\nstart that followed hit an uninstalled revision:\n\n  ERROR [o.j.s.l.BundleLicenseCheckerListener] - Invalid license check\n  Caused by: NullPointerException ... BundleRevision.getWiring() is null\n\nThe CI signing job would not have caught this: it only runs when the last\ncommit message carries [ci sign], and reports success as a no-op otherwise.\nRegenerated with keymaker-cli 2.0, which now reports the pom as valid.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqV77CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbGAQAJGgMdve3LVqBqgU6kl2gagK\nzXqACxt5nerdkW3Dmq68WTOSxliGwfxY3rr43USB8bykYvvuugDNortnEsKYMZGG\n8w2cWI/3VSFHcsR7Qy4grZTzqf29sDOiZMMaoUDmMOTiOZ28q0JefE+KOzg8ic4+\nOpKxVD3ssr09afZHvAfVwrJInpxQ6li5+70y4chGCIX++LPQt/sxz1IJcNlnSpf6\ncJoJXCYTw+0UP6t4K8I9hKWGjF1dDZTqGesvdMsuDC6dFf+t4vj6BCKiKrio3obc\nE66B41