7c341c33bf0ebb3ba9092899c9bc8ff","sha":"d3fd051747c341c33bf0ebb3ba9092899c9bc8ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/d3fd051747c341c33bf0ebb3ba9092899c9bc8ff"}],"sha":"645727421ca0231c76a620a28c193c9399da560f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/645727421ca0231c76a620a28c193c9399da560f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80773810?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheKlem","id":80773810,"login":"TheKlem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNzczODEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/d3fd051747c341c33bf0ebb3ba9092899c9bc8ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:07:06Z","email":"80773810+TheKlem@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TheKlem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:07:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: ask the node checks for the primary node type before publishing (#2755)\n\n* fix: ask the node checks for the primary node type before publishing\n\nClicking \"publication manager\" in the publication dropdown did nothing and\nthrew in the console: the action passes res.node.primaryNodeType.name to\nwindow.authoringApi.showPublicationManager, but its useNodeChecks options\nnever requested that field. useNodeInfo only adds primaryNodeType to the\ngenerated query when getPrimaryNodeType is set, so res.node.primaryNodeType\nwas undefined and reading .name threw.\n\nPresent since the action was added in ae48e7e1, so 3.4 and 3.6 are affected\ntoo - it is not a regression. The two sibling actions that read the same field\noff a useNodeChecks result, deletePermanentlyAction and subContentsAction,\nboth already request it.\n\nFixes #2715\n\n* test: cover the node checks options the publication manager click depends on\n\nThe regression is invisible at the call site: res.node.primaryNodeType.name\nreads a field that only exists when getPrimaryNodeType is passed to\nuseNodeChecks, so nothing near the onClick shows the coupling. Assert the\noption is requested - that case fails when the option is removed - and cover\nthe arguments handed to window.authoringApi.showPublicationManager.\n\n* fix: read the publication manager mixins from where the query puts them\n\ngetProperties([''jcr:mixinTypes'']) returns the mixins inside properties, as a\njcr:mixinTypes entry whose values hold the names - not as node.mixinTypes.\nThe action read node.mixinTypes off the useNodeChecks result, which is never\nselected, so the optional chaining silently produced [] and the publication\nmanager was always handed an empty mixin list.\n\nhasMixin() in JContent.utils already copes with both shapes; this is the one\ncall site that assumed the wrong one. Verified against the running instance:\nfor /sites/digitall/contents/person-portrait-1 the generated query returns\nproperties: [{name: \"jcr:mixinTypes\", values: [\"jdmix:socialIcons\",\n\"jmix:renderable\"]}] and no mixinTypes field at all.\n\nThe onClick test now mocks that real shape, so it fails on the old expression.","tree":{"sha":"eb96153e8a0dc2e24a0f1b51a6e38b914a105030","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/eb96153e8a0dc2e24a0f1b51a6e38b914a105030"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/d3fd051747c341c33bf0ebb3ba9092899c9bc8ff","verification":{"payload":"tree eb96153e8a0dc2e24a0f1b51a6e38b914a105030\nparent 0aa08becb917f72190e2a07065ddcb8a5fdd4519\nauthor TheKlem <80773810+TheKlem@users.noreply.github.com> 1788354426 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788354426 -0400\n\nfix: ask the node checks for the primary node type before publishing (#2755)\n\n* fix: ask the node checks for the primary node type before publishing\n\nClicking \"publication manager\" in the publication dropdown did nothing and\nthrew in the console: the action passes res.node.primaryNodeType.name to\nwindow.authoringApi.showPublicationManager, but its useNodeChecks options\nnever requested that field. useNodeInfo only adds primaryNodeType to the\ngenerated query when getPrimaryNodeType is set, so res.node.primaryNodeType\nwas undefined and reading .name threw.\n\nPresent since the action was added in ae48e7e1, so 3.4 and 3.6 are affected\ntoo - it is not a regression. The two sibling actions that read the same field\noff a useNodeChecks result, deletePermanentlyAction and subContentsAction,\nboth already request it.\n\nFixes #2715\n\n* test: cover the node checks options the publication manager click depends on\n\nThe regression is invisible at the call site: res.node.primaryNodeType.name\nreads a field that only exists when getPrimaryNodeType is passed to\nuseNodeChecks, so nothing near the onClick shows the coupling. Assert the\noption is requested - that case fails when the option is removed - and cover\nthe arguments handed to window.authoringApi.showPublicationManager.\n\n* fix: read the publication manager mixins from where the query puts them\n\ngetProperties([''jcr:mixinTypes'']) returns the mixins inside properties, as a\njcr:mixinTypes entry whose values hold the names - not as node.mixinTypes.\nThe action read node.mixinTypes off the useNodeChecks result, which is never\nselected, so the optional chaining silently produced [] and the publication\nmanager was always handed an empty mixin list.\n\nhasMixin() in JContent.utils already copes with both shapes; this is the one\ncall site that assumed the wrong one. Verified against the running instance:\nfor /sites/digitall/contents/person-portrait-1 the generated query returns\nproperties: [{name: \"jcr:mixinTypes\", values: [\"jdmix:socialIcons\",\n\"jmix:renderable\"]}] and no mixinTypes field at all.\n\nThe onClick test now mocks that real shape, so it fails on the old expression.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmB96CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl3gQAAQpJYgC0t4nBtHLBghdMopU\nJBFwDfVFpGvf6f8d6ovMCHPMI6by/u5uVr4RzfBdbwuqrQwNR9KFEmv+Vs3QlSeK\nAUByBywEeBscPHsAJiEoJbo/nJYSYxSc+e+bt8Il/rMZqJi8bM3pzib77WGQ7kBZ\ne7krvLG+8lamai+u5CoyxZ/8MSeprB/nlHgxtx0mhM39fYahcpsSmseoA0zZeAGz\ni1g5aQ1eZBSNPi1my1hBkQXaCId9JObvnxAyJ6iWPP/2wv1VKKHjVbgVH76WyScW\nX1AUQ3X3mkU/tQRMN5S0SA2J9xcyG3NEdFgcO+CvDe5VsZkT1O6+F7qcIGWsma4b\ncMVOHnnjVbl+LrKtnEn+xI9dXSlSsZiQzN7ROnh4/c0Jewacyv0uOVkWi8fceFV/\njIyw7/gdMyS/+TFwDk1Va7WPcq3r8Lg6K0PmLR0SCv3DThIDoNNgXHHxxGPkv6XA\ng5ic9vlSF6wZdpQ+pImJ2f8I9pXE14XSNfrZgp6FOKDNr0t5I1dA1MpCyRobc9t4\nTNFMWKG8kMElbbg//lLzPmDinN0iN3/IOtMvCe7fjt9itFmQKOozaEo5tW+rfpKw\n4hUPy/psfbvfhx2Yvs5PNmbWxgMfJQxLfnpyRraXwrJED+I0SORXoyFKVr91UeIu\nYRJJ2doAwO46WJh7JsI6\n=jhRA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T13:07:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/d3fd051747c341c33bf0ebb3ba9092899c9bc8ff","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKGQzZmQwNTE3NDdjMzQxYzMzYmYwZWJiM2JhOTA5Mjg5OWM5YmM4ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/0aa08becb917f72190e2a07065ddcb8a5fdd4519","sha":"0aa08becb917f72190e2a07065ddcb8a5fdd4519","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/0aa08becb917f72190e2a07065ddcb8a5fdd4519"}],"sha":"d3fd051747c341c33bf0ebb3ba9092899c9bc8ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/d3fd051747c341c33bf0ebb3ba9092899c9bc8ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/745718?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jkevan","id":745718,"login":"jkevan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTcxOA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkevan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/0aa08becb917f72190e2a07065ddcb8a5fdd4519/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:58:57Z","email":"kevan@jahia.com","name":"kevan Jahanshahi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:58:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: retire the visibility module from jContent''s own activator (#2752)\n\n* fix: retire the visibility module from jContent''s own activator\n\nUpgrading jContent moves the visibility condition node types over to it,\nand 05-migrateVisibilityConditions.resolved.groovy does that part. What it\ncannot do is remove the module they came from. Uninstalling that module\nafterwards tears down the condition rules, the background actions and the\nrules package jContent has by then registered under the same node type\nnames, because VisibilityService.removeCondition matches on the node type\nname alone and does not check which module registered it. The script says\nso itself and points at a separate migrator module to install alongside.\n\njContent can do it without one. Two properties make the difference.\n\nWhen: a bundle''s own activator is called from inside Felix.startBundle,\nbefore the STARTED event that makes the module extender register the\npackage, its rules and its observers. That is the last moment at which the\nnode types have moved and jContent has registered nothing an uninstall\ncould tear down.\n\nHow: Bundle.stop() and Bundle.uninstall() act on this node only. They do\nnot go through ModuleManager, so there is no cluster operation to wait for.\nThat matters beyond tidiness. A clustered uninstall asked for from a module\nlifecycle callback does not complete, because Jahia gives Karaf Cellar''s\nevent dispatcher a single worker thread and the caller is occupying it; it\ntimes out after about three minutes and leaves the nodes disagreeing. The\nlocal call has nothing to wait for, and every node runs its own activator,\nso every node removes its own copy.\n\nDeliberately not guarded by an \"already migrated\" flag. Such a flag would\nhave to be shared across the cluster, and a node that was down during the\nmigration would read it, skip, and come back still carrying the module the\nothers removed. So this also removes a source installed after the\nmigration, which is correct rather than incidental: both modules declare\nthe same condition node types, only one can own them, and whichever\nregisters second has its definitions ignored. The removal logs at WARN.\n\nMeasured on a two-node cellar cluster, from the state a customer upgrades\nfrom: jContent 3.6.0 and visibility 9.0.0 both active, visibility owning\nthe node types. After the upgrade, in this order, the script moves the\nthree node types and redeploys the definitions, the activator removes\nvisibility in 50ms, and only then does jContent start. visibility and\nadvanced-visibility are gone from both nodes, jContent is ACTIVE on both,\nand no restart is needed. Re-running the upgrade with nothing to remove and\nrestarting a node are both clean no-ops.\n\nOnce no supported upgrade path still has a source installed, this class and\nits call in the activator can go.\n\n* fix: keep watching for the source module, and correct the ordering claim\n\nCode review of the first commit found nine things. Two of them were the\ngaps that made the separate migrator module worth having, and this closes\nboth. Two others were mine to correct.\n\nThe migrator listened for a source being installed AFTER the migration and\nremoved it there and then. Without that, a source that turns up later - a\nrestore, a provisioning script, a jar dropped in the modules folder - sits\nactive until the next start of jContent, which may be months. A synchronous\nlistener now removes it as it arrives. Measured: 1ms.\n\nThe migrator also listened for a source being STOPPED rather than removed,\nand re-registered the target''s condition rules. That matters because\nVisibilityService.removeCondition matches on the node type name alone, so\nstopping a source unregisters the rules jContent published under those same\nnames, silently, and nothing else puts them back. Re-publishing what\njContent still has registered as OSGi services undoes it.\n\nThe ordering claim in the javadoc was wrong, and it is the sentence the\nwhole design rests on. The extender''s resolve() already registers the\npackage and deploys the definitions, on RESOLVED, before this activator\nruns. Only the condition rules are registered later, on STARTED. The\nconclusion holds - the rules are what an uninstall of the source tears down\n- but the reason had to be stated correctly.\n\nAlso documents an asymmetry that was load-bearing and unwritten: the\nnode-type handover is a patch script and the extender only runs those on\nthe processing server, while this class runs on every node because every\nnode has its own copy of the bundle to remove. A browsing node therefore\nremoves a module whose types it never re-owned locally, which is correct,\nbecause its definitions come from the database.\n\nDurations use nanoTime rather than currentTimeMillis, which is the right\nclock for a duration.\n\nTwo of the review''s findings did not reproduce on a two-node cluster and\nare left alone: the cluster bundle map does not retain the locally removed\nmodule, and no jar is left in the modules folder, so a node restart does\nnot bring it back. Verified by reading the Cellar map and by restarting a\nnode. That was measured for a module installed through provisioning; a jar\nplaced in the modules folder by hand is a path the new listener now covers\nanyway.\n\n* docs: the migration script no longer sends the reader to a separate module\n\n05-migrateVisibilityConditions.resolved.groovy told the operator to install\nvisibility-migrator, and its header called removing the source beforehand a\nprerequisite. Neither holds now that jContent removes the source itself, and\na message that sends someone to install a module they do not need is worse\nthan no message.\n\nThe warning becomes an INFO that says what happens next: jContent removes\nthe source from this node as it starts, before registering the condition\nrules. WARN was right when there was a hazard the script could not prevent;\nthere is nothing for the reader to do now, and the activator already logs\nat WARN when it removes something.\n\nThe header keeps the one fact an operator still needs. Removing the source\nby hand works, at the cost of a window in which no visibility condition is\nevaluated, and leaving it in place has no such window because the handover\nhere and the removal there happen within the same bundle start.\n\nRe-measured on a FOUR node cluster, one processing and three browsing, from\njContent 3.6.0 with visibility 9.0.0 active on all four. The script switches\nthe three node types once on the processing node, then each of the four\nnodes removes its own copy - 137, 64, 67 and 47 ms - and only then does\njContent start. Four removals for four nodes, no activator error anywhere,\nvisibility and advanced-visibility gone from all four, jContent ACTIVE on\nall four.\n\n* refactor: drop the visibility watch and the node type check\n\nTwo pieces of the retirement were doing no work.\n\ndeclaresConditionTypes read jContent''s own CND to decide whether jContent owns\nthe condition node types. The class ships inside the jar it was reading, so the\nanswer was fixed at build time for that build, and this build does declare them.\nThe check could only ever return true, and it read the wrong thing to do so.\n\nwatch registered a bundle listener that stayed for the life of jContent, to\nremove a source module installed again after the migration. Nobody asked for\nthat guard. Reinstalling a retired source is a deliberate act, and jContent has\nno business policing it forever. The two triggers the review worried about were\ntested on a four-node cluster and neither reproduces: the Cellar bundle map\nholds no entry after the local uninstall, and restarting a node does not bring\nthe module back.\n\nWhat that window still leaves open is written down in the class javadoc instead\nof guarded in code.\n\n* fix: evaluate the removal summary only when the warning is logged\n\nSonar S2629 on the WARN in retireSources: names(present) is invoked whatever\nthe log level, because SLF4J evaluates the arguments before it decides to\nwrite. The call is cheap, and the rule is about the habit rather than this\none cost, so it is guarded like any other.\n\n* fix: take the review''s findings on ordering, failure handling and the changelog\n\nAn adversarial review of this branch raised ten findings. Six were real, and\nthis commit takes all six. The rest are answered in the PR, one of them with\na cluster run.\n\nRemoval order. SOURCES lists advanced-visibility before visibility, which\nreads as dependency-safe, but findSources iterated context.getBundles() and\nreturned bundle-id order instead. visibility is installed first, so it had\nthe lower id and was removed first. findSources now iterates SOURCES, so the\nlist means what it looks like it means.\n\nA failed stop no longer skips the uninstall. The two calls shared one try, so\na BundleException from stop() left the source installed and active, which is\nthe exact state this class exists to prevent. uninstall() stops an active\nbundle itself, so it is now attempted either way.\n\nThe call site catches Throwable. retireSources catches Exception, but the\nfirst reference to the class runs its static initialisation at the call site,\noutside that handler. A LinkageError there would abort jContent''s start, which\nthe class javadoc promises cannot happen.\n\nThe javadoc named the wrong mechanism. The condition rules are Declarative\nServices components bound through an osgi:list in the Spring bridge, not\nsomething the extender registers on the STARTED event. The timing conclusion\nis unchanged and the reasoning now points at the code that implements it.\n\nIt also claimed too much. A local uninstall is not invisible to the cluster:\non the processing server the extender schedules clearModuleNodes, which\ndeletes the module''s nodes in the shared repository, on a Quartz thread and\noutside this class''s error handling. That is written down now, along with the\nfailed-removal gap.\n\nChangelog. 6aFGuZWf.md is unreleased on main and told customers to install\nvisibility-migrator before upgrading, which this change makes wrong; it now\ndescribes only what #2726 did. This branch''s own note was a 168-character\npatch entry for a change that uninstalls a module on every node, so it is a\nminor bump written as the breaking change it is.\n\nThe NOSONAR on uninstallLocally is gone with the generic catch it excused.\n\n* fix: retry a contended uninstall, name the stranded modules, fold the changelog\n\nFour points from the review.\n\nUninstalling needs the framework''s global lock, and this thread holds\njContent''s bundle lock while asking for it. Felix refuses that combination\nrather than deadlocking, so a provisioning batch installing modules at the\nsame moment can make the attempt fail with an IllegalStateException. That is\ncontention, not a defect, so the removal is retried three times with a 200 ms\nwait. The retries stay small because this runs inside jContent''s start. The\nerror that follows exhausted retries now tells the operator how to recover.\n\nRemoving a source strands anything that declared a dependency on it. The\nextender parks a module whose declared dependency has no registered version\nand never resolves it again, and visibility is a public module a custom one\nmay legitimately depend on. Those modules are now named in the log before the\nremoval, read from the Jahia-Depends manifest header rather than from\nTemplatePackageRegistry, which does not yet know jContent at this point.\n\nThe removal-order rationale claimed advanced-visibility could be wired to\nvisibility. It is not: its pom declares no jahia-depends on it and nothing\nunder its src imports the package. The order is still worth fixing, so the\ncomment now says what it actually buys, which is independence from install\norder.\n\n6aFGuZWf.md is folded into this branch''s fragment and deleted. Both were\nunreleased and described the same migration, so the release notes would have\ncarried two entries for it. The surviving text keeps the #2726 reference and\nadds the dependency warning.\n\n* revert: drop the dependent-module warning, keep it in the release note\n\nA module declaring Jahia-Depends on visibility is parked by the extender once\nvisibility is gone, and never resolved again. That is true of any removal:\nthis activator, the visibility-migrator module, or an operator uninstalling it\nby hand. It follows from retiring visibility, which #2724 decided, and not\nfrom how this class removes it.\n\nThe warning also fired too late to act on. It printed during jContent''s start,\nin the same breath as the removal, when nothing can be done about it. The\noperator needs that before the upgrade, and the release note carries it there.\n\nIt was untested as well. No run exercised it, so it added a path nobody had\nseen work to a class whose value is being small and deletable.\n\nThe ATTEMPTS and BACKOFF_MS constants move up with the other fields while the\nfile is open.\n\n* style: close the two gaps the reverted paragraph left behind\n\nRemoving the dependent-module paragraph left a bare blank line inside the\njavadoc block, and removing dependentsOf left a blank line above the closing\nbrace.\n\n* fix: name the broken functionality and the recovery order in the give-up error\n\nThe error logged when the retries are exhausted said the condition rules\nwould be torn down, without naming what stops working or in which order\nto recover. It now states that visibility conditions break on this node,\nwhy unbinding either module drops them, and that the uninstall comes\nbefore the jContent redeploy.\n\nAlso folds names() into a stream, which reads shorter for the same work.","tree":{"sha":"4dd8f142dc1291ebb70bcdf7cdd1037c6935f85f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/4dd8f142dc1291ebb70bcdf7cdd1037c6935f85f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/0aa08becb917f72190e2a07065ddcb8a5fdd4519","verification":{"payload":"tree 4dd8f142dc1291ebb70bcdf7cdd1037c6935f85f\nparent 382d4c5b5fd431503799a5d44a8833a707592f78\nauthor kevan Jahanshahi <kevan@jahia.com> 1788353937 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788353937 +0200\n\nfix: retire the visibility module from jContent''s own activator (#2752)\n\n* fix: retire the visibility module from jContent''s own activator\n\nUpgrading jContent moves the visibility condition node types over to it,\nand 05-migrateVisibilityConditions.resolved.groovy does that part. What it\ncannot do is remove the module they came from. Uninstalling that module\nafterwards tears down the condition rules, the background actions and the\nrules package jContent has by then registered under the same node type\nnames, because VisibilityService.removeCondition matches on the node type\nname alone and does not check which module registered it. The script says\nso itself and points at a separate migrator module to install alongside.\n\njContent can do it without one. Two properties make the difference.\n\nWhen: a bundle''s own activator is called from inside Felix.startBundle,\nbefore the STARTED event that makes the module extender register the\npackage, its rules and its observers. That is the last moment at which the\nnode types have moved and jContent has registered nothing an uninstall\ncould tear down.\n\nHow: Bundle.stop() and Bundle.uninstall() act on this node only. They do\nnot go through ModuleManager, so there is no cluster operation to wait for.\nThat matters beyond tidiness. A clustered uninstall asked for from a module\nlifecycle callback does not complete, because Jahia gives Karaf Cellar''s\nevent dispatcher a single worker thread and the caller is occupying it; it\ntimes out after about three minutes and leaves the nodes disagreeing. The\nlocal call has nothing to wait for, and every node runs its own activator,\nso every node removes its own copy.\n\nDeliberately not guarded by an \"already migrated\" flag. Such a flag would\nhave to be shared across the cluster, and a node that was down during the\nmigration would read it, skip, and come back still carrying the module the\nothers removed. So this also removes a source installed after the\nmigration, which is correct rather than incidental: both modules declare\nthe same condition node types, only one can own them, and whichever\nregisters second has its definitions ignored. The removal logs at WARN.\n\nMeasured on a two-node cellar cluster, from the state a customer upgrades\nfrom: jContent 3.6.0 and visibility 9.0.0 both active, visibility owning\nthe node types. After the upgrade, in this order, the script moves the\nthree node types and redeploys the definitions, the activator removes\nvisibility in 50ms, and only then does jContent start. visibility and\nadvanced-visibility are gone from both nodes, jContent is ACTIVE on both,\nand no restart is needed. Re-running the upgrade with nothing to remove and\nrestarting a node are both clean no-ops.\n\nOnce no supported upgrade path still has a source installed, this class and\nits call in the activator can go.\n\n* fix: keep watching for the source module, and correct the ordering claim\n\nCode review of the first commit found nine things. Two of them were the\ngaps that made the separate migrator module worth having, and this closes\nboth. Two others were mine to correct.\n\nThe migrator listened for a source being installed AFTER the migration and\nremoved it there and then. Without that, a source that turns up later - a\nrestore, a provisioning script, a jar dropped in the modules folder - sits\nactive until the next start of jContent, which may be months. A synchronous\nlistener now removes it as it arrives. Measured: 1ms.\n\nThe migrator also listened for a source being STOPPED rather than removed,\nand re-registered the target''s condition rules. That matters because\nVisibilityService.removeCondition matches on the node type name alone, so\nstopping a source unregisters the rules jContent published under those same\nnames, silently, and nothing else puts them back. Re-publishing what\njContent still has registered as OSGi services undoes it.\n\nThe ordering claim in the javadoc was wrong, and it is the sentence the\nwhole design rests on. The extender''s resolve() already registers the\npackage and deploys the definitions, on RESOLVED, before this activator\nruns. Only the condition rules are registered later, on STARTED. The\nconclusion holds - the rules are what an uninstall of the source tears down\n- but the reason had to be stated correctly.\n\nAlso documents an asymmetry that was load-bearing and unwritten: the\nnode-type handover is a patch script and the extender only runs those on\nthe processing server, while this class runs on every node because every\nnode has its own copy of the bundle to remove. A browsing node therefore\nremoves a module whose types it never re-owned locally, which is correct,\nbecause its definitions come from the database.\n\nDurations use nanoTime rather than currentTimeMillis, which is the right\nclock for a duration.\n\nTwo of the review''s findings did not reproduce on a two-node cluster and\nare left alone: the cluster bundle map does not retain the locally removed\nmodule, and no jar is left in the modules folder, so a node restart does\nnot bring it back. Verified by reading the Cellar map and by restarting a\nnode. That was measured for a module installed through provisioning; a jar\nplaced in the modules folder by hand is a path the new listener now covers\nanyway.\n\n* docs: the migration script no longer sends the reader to a separate module\n\n05-migrateVisibilityConditions.resolved.groovy told the operator to install\nvisibility-migrator, and its header called removing the source beforehand a\nprerequisite. Neither holds now that jContent removes the source itself, and\na message that sends someone to install a module they do not need is worse\nthan no message.\n\nThe warning becomes an INFO that says what happens next: jContent removes\nthe source from this node as it starts, before registering the condition\nrules. WARN was right when there was a hazard the script could not prevent;\nthere is nothing for the reader to do now, and the activator already logs\nat WARN when it removes something.\n\nThe header keeps the one fact an operator still needs. Removing the source\nby hand works, at the cost of a window in which no visibility condition is\nevaluated, and leaving it in place has no such window because the handover\nhere and the removal there happen within the same bundle start.\n\nRe-measured on a FOUR node cluster, one processing and three browsing, from\njContent 3.6.0 with visibility 9.0.0 active on all four. The script switches\nthe three node types once on the processing node, then each of the four\nnodes removes its own copy - 137, 64, 67 and 47 ms - and only then does\njContent start. Four removals for four nodes, no activator error anywhere,\nvisibility and advanced-visibility gone from all four, jContent ACTIVE on\nall four.\n\n* refactor: drop the visibility watch and the node type check\n\nTwo pieces of the retirement were doing no work.\n\ndeclaresConditionTypes read jContent''s own CND to decide whether jContent owns\nthe condition node types. The class ships inside the jar it was reading, so the\nanswer was fixed at build time for that build, and this build does declare them.\nThe check could only ever return true, and it read the wrong thing to do so.\n\nwatch registered a bundle listener that stayed for the life of jContent, to\nremove a source module installed again after the migration. Nobody asked for\nthat guard. Reinstalling a retired source is a deliberate act, and jContent has\nno business policing it forever. The two triggers the review worried about were\ntested on a four-node cluster and neither reproduces: the Cellar bundle map\nholds no entry after the local uninstall, and restarting a node does not bring\nthe module back.\n\nWhat that window still leaves open is written down in the class javadoc instead\nof guarded in code.\n\n* fix: evaluate the removal summary only when the warning is logged\n\nSonar S2629 on the WARN in retireSources: names(present) is invoked whatever\nthe log level, because SLF4J evaluates the arguments before it decides to\nwrite. The call is cheap, and the rule is about the habit rather than this\none cost, so it is guarded like any other.\n\n* fix: take the review''s findings on ordering, failure handling and the changelog\n\nAn adversarial review of this branch raised ten findings. Six were real, and\nthis commit takes all six. The rest are answered in the PR, one of them with\na cluster run.\n\nRemoval order. SOURCES lists advanced-visibility before visibility, which\nreads as dependency-safe, but findSources iterated context.getBundles() and\nreturned bundle-id order instead. visibility is installed first, so it had\nthe lower id and was removed first. findSources now iterates SOURCES, so the\nlist means what it looks like it means.\n\nA failed stop no longer skips the uninstall. The two calls shared one try, so\na BundleException from stop() left the source installed and active, which is\nthe exact state this class exists to prevent. uninstall() stops an active\nbundle itself, so it is now attempted either way.\n\nThe call site catches Throwable. retireSources catches Exception, but the\nfirst reference to the class runs its static initialisation at the call site,\noutside that handler. A LinkageError there would abort jContent''s start, which\nthe class javadoc promises cannot happen.\n\nThe javadoc named the wrong mechanism. The condition rules are Declarative\nServices components bound through an osgi:list in the Spring bridge, not\nsomething the extender registers on the STARTED event. The timing conclusion\nis unchanged and the reasoning now points at the code that implements it.\n\nIt also claimed too much. A local uninstall is not invisible to the cluster:\non the processing server the extender schedules clearModuleNodes, which\ndeletes the module''s nodes in the shared repository, on a Quartz thread and\noutside this class''s error handling. That is written down now, along with the\nfailed-removal gap.\n\nChangelog. 6aFGuZWf.md is unreleased on main and told customers to install\nvisibility-migrator before upgrading, which this change makes wrong; it now\ndescribes only what #2726 did. This branch''s own note was a 168-character\npatch entry for a change that uninstalls a module on every node, so it is a\nminor bump written as the breaking change it is.\n\nThe NOSONAR on uninstallLocally is gone with the generic catch it excused.\n\n* fix: retry a contended uninstall, name the stranded modules, fold the changelog\n\nFour points from the review.\n\nUninstalling needs the framework''s global lock, and this thread holds\njContent''s bundle lock while asking for it. Felix refuses that combination\nrather than deadlocking, so a provisioning batch installing modules at the\nsame moment can make the attempt fail with an IllegalStateException. That is\ncontention, not a defect, so the removal is retried three times with a 200 ms\nwait. The retries stay small because this runs inside jContent''s start. The\nerror that follows exhausted retries now tells the operator how to recover.\n\nRemoving a source strands anything that declared a dependency on it. The\nextender parks a module whose declared dependency has no registered version\nand never resolves it again, and visibility is a public module a custom one\nmay legitimately depend on. Those modules are now named in the log before the\nremoval, read from the Jahia-Depends manifest header rather than from\nTemplatePackageRegistry, which does not yet know jContent at this point.\n\nThe removal-order rationale claimed advanced-visibility could be wired to\nvisibility. It is not: its pom declares no jahia-depends on it and nothing\nunder its src imports the package. The order is still worth fixing, so the\ncomment now says what it actually buys, which is independence from install\norder.\n\n6aFGuZWf.md is folded into this branch''s fragment and deleted. Both were\nunreleased and described the same migration, so the release notes would have\ncarried two entries for it. The surviving text keeps the #2726 reference and\nadds the dependency warning.\n\n* revert: drop the dependent-module warning, keep it in the release note\n\nA module declaring Jahia-Depends on visibility is parked by the extender once\nvisibility is gone, and never resolved again. That is true of any removal:\nthis activator, the visibility-migrator module, or an operator uninstalling it\nby hand. It follows from retiring visibility, which #2724 decided, and not\nfrom how this class removes it.\n\nThe warning also fired too late to act on. It printed during jContent''s start,\nin the same breath as the removal, when nothing can be done about it. The\noperator needs that before the upgrade, and the release note carries it there.\n\nIt was untested as well. No run exercised it, so it added a path nobody had\nseen work to a class whose value is being small and deletable.\n\nThe ATTEMPTS and BACKOFF_MS constants move up with the other fields while the\nfile is open.\n\n* style: close the two gaps the reverted paragraph left behind\n\nRemoving the dependent-module paragraph left a bare blank line inside the\njavadoc block, and removing dependentsOf left a blank line above the closing\nbrace.\n\n* fix: name the broken functionality and the recovery order in the give-up error\n\nThe error logged when the retries are exhausted said the condition rules\nwould be torn down, without naming what stops working or in which order\nto recover. It now states that visibility conditions break on this node,\nwhy unbinding either module drops them, and that the uninstall comes\nbefore the jContent redeploy.\n\nAlso folds names() into a stream, which reads shorter for the same work.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmB2RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADHUQAJaJ7aPcHWXWz3DtGB32UaXJ\nOVI9ayDq66qPelsLc+dB8KtafS42ELdNK/gU1M2sJNP4PdCFsE75eRupR944bQkW\ndRs3SDJElc+GnQdVIWbLgbKyZIt4NalHQgMwPsjr9qfHH3Drs0GAZnWIunQmoBJa\nCKm/9hX3HcXgwPxN9/pT9GlVjXvexPKJg6EiLxM4nhBBnge2rqMSJGBTXpXX1B59\nOInLNJFlNWdOBotiRuZgeoHyruTLbPJEj81Rn662taE/2jubNbpTpCigtRvBu49J\n/166OO1R/uGZ//l/iJPrOGSO54rxjL8A7Ipvro2Wg1D8R8XLkt/J7+UuDit9CVMf\nlx9ngdRJPvGfYKFg0ze4uvKiUj0QwQLRwjoXyO55DHM3AWWcRukKwzbhdXxcGAjh\nADMokCPWZnjekd/bAgrdBMRms38E9F3dzWWU8AnwR7aXgyLbYPjrsYcerQfGs1x5\nlbYYD10KUjxPS+XAtom7O70lvevlKG0dFpI9Pib+H5lW1WE/EbhQ1cTxM3W6BQSG\nSkEWj5SCFKN4JENQHWtfuy4pA9V1a54+wDkYpBp7yoUkId8il0ksFkwJo2Aw4fq2\nVfK5fXgvKA28ufdG4G/8rEVshlk3KmdZW5aVT/cQ0E1WHMtoQxe7r8Am5iEjoYDl\nlxNaIlPBQ8xeALvEny83\n=UWH/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T12:58:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/0aa08becb917f72190e2a07065ddcb8a5fdd4519","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKDBhYTA4YmVjYjkxN2Y3MjE5MGUyYTA3MDY1ZGRjYjhhNWZkZDQ1MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/382d4c5b5fd431503799a5d44a8833a707592f78","sha":"382d4c5b5fd431503799a5d44a8833a707592f78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/382d4c5b5fd431503799a5d44a8833a707592f78"}],"sha":"0aa08becb917f72190e2a07065ddcb8a5fdd4519","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/0aa08becb917f72190e2a07065ddcb8a5fdd4519"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80773810?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheKlem","id":80773810,"login":"TheKlem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNzczODEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheKlem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/382d4c5b5fd431503799a5d44a8833a707592f78/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:08:27Z","email":"80773810+TheKlem@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TheKlem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:08:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: sort content types by display name, not system name (#2750)\n\ngetContentTypesAsTree sorted its top-level entries with\nComparator.comparing(GqlNodeTypeTreeEntry::getName), i.e. by system name,\nwhile the Select Content Type dialog renders the list exactly as received\n(ContentTypeSelectorModal does no client-side sorting). Contributors\ntherefore read labels ordered by the technical names behind them:\n\n    Input Checkbox      (fmdb:checkbox)\n    Block Fieldset      (fmdb:fieldset)     <- between two \"Input ...\" entries\n    Input Button        (fmdb:inputButton)\n\nAny module whose labels do not happen to share the alphabetical order of\nits type names is affected, and translated labels make it worse.\n\nNodeTypeTreeEntry already defines exactly the wanted ordering as its\nnatural order:\n\n    public int compareTo(NodeTypeTreeEntry other) {\n        return StringUtils.compareIgnoreCase(getLabel(), other.getLabel());\n    }\n\nso the explicit comparator is dropped in favour of sorting the entries\nbefore wrapping them. GqlNodeTypeTreeEntry.getChildren() was already\nsorting by label and is switched to the same natural order, which makes\nthe whole tree consistent and the comparison case-insensitive at every\nlevel rather than only below the first.\n\nRegression from c52136df (#2287).\n\nFixes #2747","tree":{"sha":"c69b6c3a917dd2721e34f406398df05cdbcd0c93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/c69b6c3a917dd2721e34f406398df05cdbcd0c93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/382d4c5b5fd431503799a5d44a8833a707592f78","verification":{"payload":"tree c69b6c3a917dd2721e34f406398df05cdbcd0c93\nparent bc1da0e9a0f144a1eb81b6f607406ce6857b35f7\nauthor TheKlem <80773810+TheKlem@users.noreply.github.com> 1788282507 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788282507 -0400\n\nfix: sort content types by display name, not system name (#2750)\n\ngetContentTypesAsTree sorted its top-level entries with\nComparator.comparing(GqlNodeTypeTreeEntry::getName), i.e. by system name,\nwhile the Select Content Type dialog renders the list exactly as received\n(ContentTypeSelectorModal does no client-side sorting). Contributors\ntherefore read labels ordered by the technical names behind them:\n\n    Input Checkbox      (fmdb:checkbox)\n    Block Fieldset      (fmdb:fieldset)     <- between two \"Input ...\" entries\n    Input Button        (fmdb:inputButton)\n\nAny module whose labels do not happen to share the alphabetical order of\nits type names is affected, and translated labels make it worse.\n\nNodeTypeTreeEntry already defines exactly the wanted ordering as its\nnatural order:\n\n    public int compareTo(NodeTypeTreeEntry other) {\n        return StringUtils.compareIgnoreCase(getLabel(), other.getLabel());\n    }\n\nso the explicit comparator is dropped in favour of sorting the entries\nbefore wrapping them. GqlNodeTypeTreeEntry.getChildren() was already\nsorting by label and is switched to the same natural order, which makes\nthe whole tree consistent and the comparison case-insensitive at every\nlevel rather than only below the first.\n\nRegression from c52136df (#2287).\n\nFixes #2747","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlwaLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgjQQAKRm/mbVpR3Fgpc0T4XcO3M2\nlfYK4UuJX2ubupFK5PbwveIunENs6jZ8tes7ob4bIm6Q29P7Qg2nzkki1oAriSf7\nW8l74jNCOcufivK73D6b4czDb4xVMRJSBsOxY39DxJoC9xcZ0Prr30+Ve7uaoWhI\nnqVxRRKjKxlpup32b1qRLXTsL5smn1mCRn0KAD3QhS8pF6xoyYNGtD5Q0IZ5jtnI\nNDwsHlY3/81ecXn0iiMX6kY/33X7Hb4oCfKf6X7Ks/GoMGLGhYWxuELV8jCgR5gR\nXRw5cVV1Se8YVHcPXFit2kqR9gTWhjF6haORcRu2v2hSs09JPCGSSOVAwvU3TlGs\nEbhu9Gc8O2X9bJF+SaZiZG9ANE8lP/Lm6og67i3zSJ7OLt7ExXV10jDQmAKdYXZx\noUhQGDlAbZ9LpMIg1cDZ017ZrGSMKHzGFSy8cYRo0lxxn56kmun/UGKdvJp8/zly\niH6y47hhc7gg1vU1vb5UzHJDueuIY27IzsPgis7x9MeZ1EmYxgNriy9xdBCGpgTe\nZbXQvajssZzbPrjkbQkhZzF8j48Cz03//O+CHkTprFZbDtzasbQm4TWyQedWBpzZ\nvoFAZVvcYmq07pPncVTUXjzqHHHdOKRxeuYcfOioe2ssASnzbJB8COyjUajbj5F2\n402hYC7jqvy+N3O9f27e\n=sR0Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T17:08:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/382d4c5b5fd431503799a5d44a8833a707592f78","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKDM4MmQ0YzViNWZkNDMxNTAzNzk5YTVkNDRhODgzM2E3MDc1OTJmNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/bc1da0e9a0f144a1eb81b6f607406ce6857b35f7","sha":"bc1da0e9a0f144a1eb81b6f607406ce6857b35f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/bc1da0e9a0f144a1eb81b6f607406ce6857b35f7"}],"sha":"382d4c5b5fd431503799a5d44a8833a707592f78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/382d4c5b5fd431503799a5d44a8833a707592f78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75278792?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gflores-jahia","id":75278792,"login":"gflores-jahia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1Mjc4Nzky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/bc1da0e9a0f144a1eb81b6f607406ce6857b35f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:52:28Z","email":"75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Geofrey Flores"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:52:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: stop language switch from copying unsaved text into the new language (#2738)\n\n* fix: stop language switch from copying unsaved text into the new language\n\nSwitching languages in the content editor while creating content carried the\ntext typed for the previous language into the new one, and saved it there.\n\nI18nContextHandler rebuilds the form values on a language change using the\nlive formik values as its base. That base is only safe when the form has just\nbeen remounted for the new language, which is what used to happen: the\nlanguage-switch refetch set loading=true and the context returned a\nLoaderOverlay, tearing Formik down and rebuilding it from initialValues.\n\nSince #2447 removed that remount to keep the switch flash-free, the form stays\nmounted and formik.values still holds the previous language''s text. For a\nlanguage never visited before, i18nContext[lang] is undefined and overwrites\nnothing, so the text survives into the new language. Edit mode was spared\nbecause #2447 also added enableReinitialize there; create mode has no\nequivalent, as its initialValues reference never changes.\n\nReset the i18n-scoped fields to their initial value before applying the target\nlanguage''s stored edits, so the handler no longer depends on a remount that no\nlonger happens.\n\n* Add language guard when copying; delete fields if non-existent\n\n* cleanup","tree":{"sha":"15b3a6d6bd3ba968b8714a38cfa49494aae20bd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/15b3a6d6bd3ba968b8714a38cfa49494aae20bd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/bc1da0e9a0f144a1eb81b6f607406ce6857b35f7","verification":{"payload":"tree 15b3a6d6bd3ba968b8714a38cfa49494aae20bd9\nparent 6cc08b1cde144878d28e81ee0287879406dc5173\nauthor Geofrey Flores <75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com> 1788281548 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788281548 -0400\n\nfix: stop language switch from copying unsaved text into the new language (#2738)\n\n* fix: stop language switch from copying unsaved text into the new language\n\nSwitching languages in the content editor while creating content carried the\ntext typed for the previous language into the new one, and saved it there.\n\nI18nContextHandler rebuilds the form values on a language change using the\nlive formik values as its base. That base is only safe when the form has just\nbeen remounted for the new language, which is what used to happen: the\nlanguage-switch refetch set loading=true and the context returned a\nLoaderOverlay, tearing Formik down and rebuilding it from initialValues.\n\nSince #2447 removed that remount to keep the switch flash-free, the form stays\nmounted and formik.values still holds the previous language''s text. For a\nlanguage never visited before, i18nContext[lang] is undefined and overwrites\nnothing, so the text survives into the new language. Edit mode was spared\nbecause #2447 also added enableReinitialize there; create mode has no\nequivalent, as its initialValues reference never changes.\n\nReset the i18n-scoped fields to their initial value before applying the target\nlanguage''s stored edits, so the handler no longer depends on a remount that no\nlonger happens.\n\n* Add language guard when copying; delete fields if non-existent\n\n* cleanup","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlwLMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzwEQAB25FwRDFV/k5uDSxhpSs6Rm\n3y/2ua8WwSZYQYi7EfqI5pH3voX0nbESJpDiM9+u47iYxKmqBTpTf7K47gCPG5kU\nLAYvMZFSE6BlqM7H/Oi3SmzMSLa8vi9TbPWo0ENrhInJhMJmBNGNBR0QqIeRmcG1\nbop4xNikr/4kTD8xsbtXwHFP/VlC+Fr3vXebZJQcoWATVICtCvlGW4Cde0GnGHSa\nxW4eWVki1CQ0s1fYknIycrPvdhq2YbFKeDZfEkVVSwbMLg3LZkLSY8CRkJP/mUv8\nLZytxeHq3zW7FG3aiSHfqRv1UiwFMkWpiDjFud+AYg3W97zxbtVfKJ+bTkxo65vq\nV6FtwHgdK+OSufNoTCElfEA0vIk9seUfcLVOBsVRdn32BOxTAh3Q+wrxcfkIxZ4u\nlolzKooouZNbSw5SobV3ujUt/CXxWFbHsHms22vy9VBFtw0zAbnlU6+13v8XWDLN\n0fliVVlg6Ova6XeFcrEZXnX6WpaktRUqybLL1kn7gG+LvRwbN+ISP8r6Uo4dr4gg\ngMHsRD1iV/M6wXcPaDLmMo/30EXmLD3NCWShaPEcLip7rMSflMJfxWpl6d4wwJpB\nAFF4e701aGDxH/b8GEWMho2xbXvCnCYVgMkJg869RMwQqjVkL7EO0TloAbgEgbgI\nd/zQl3i2lxNWVOQJd0uJ\n=BIJg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:52:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/bc1da0e9a0f144a1eb81b6f607406ce6857b35f7","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKGJjMWRhMGU5YTBmMTQ0YTFlYjgxYjZmNjA3NDA2Y2U2ODU3YjM1Zjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/6cc08b1cde144878d28e81ee0287879406dc5173","sha":"6cc08b1cde144878d28e81ee0287879406dc5173","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/6cc08b1cde144878d28e81ee0287879406dc5173"}],"sha":"bc1da0e9a0f144a1eb81b6f607406ce6857b35f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/bc1da0e9a0f144a1eb81b6f607406ce6857b35f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75278792?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gflores-jahia","id":75278792,"login":"gflores-jahia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1Mjc4Nzky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/6cc08b1cde144878d28e81ee0287879406dc5173/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:47:21Z","email":"75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Geofrey Flores"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:47:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Remove cluster uninstall and make it as an external prerequisite (#2745)\n\nUninstalling the legacy visibility module from inside jContent''s own\ndeployment tore down the condition rules jContent had just registered for\nthe same node types. The core removes a condition by node type name alone,\nso unregistering visibility''s rules dropped jContent''s, leaving the node\ntypes with no rule at all - and an empty rule set makes matchesConditions\nreturn true, so every conditioned item rendered unconditionally, with\nnothing logged.\n\nRemoving the legacy modules moves out to the separate visibility-migrator\nmodule, which does it before jContent activates, so there is nothing of\njContent''s to evict. What remains here only switches ownership of the\ncondition node types, synchronously, and refuses with an explicit error\nwhile a legacy module is still installed.\n\nThe script is renamed because the patcher keys its status on the entry\npath: 3.7.0 shipped a script at the old path that always recorded\n\".installed\", so a rewrite under that name would be filtered out on every\ninstall that already ran it.","tree":{"sha":"a37e6fb3c07d726a2ee8f344b0295adda88ba010","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/trees/a37e6fb3c07d726a2ee8f344b0295adda88ba010"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/git/commits/6cc08b1cde144878d28e81ee0287879406dc5173","verification":{"payload":"tree a37e6fb3c07d726a2ee8f344b0295adda88ba010\nparent 2a0341203a90f59a581569e0cd184a3ddc8579dc\nauthor Geofrey Flores <75278792+gflores-jahia@users.noreply.github.com> 1788180441 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788180441 -0400\n\nfix: Remove cluster uninstall and make it as an external prerequisite (#2745)\n\nUninstalling the legacy visibility module from inside jContent''s own\ndeployment tore down the condition rules jContent had just registered for\nthe same node types. The core removes a condition by node type name alone,\nso unregistering visibility''s rules dropped jContent''s, leaving the node\ntypes with no rule at all - and an empty rule set makes matchesConditions\nreturn true, so every conditioned item rendered unconditionally, with\nnothing logged.\n\nRemoving the legacy modules moves out to the separate visibility-migrator\nmodule, which does it before jContent activates, so there is nothing of\njContent''s to evict. What remains here only switches ownership of the\ncondition node types, synchronously, and refuses with an explicit error\nwhile a legacy module is still installed.\n\nThe script is renamed because the patcher keys its status on the entry\npath: 3.7.0 shipped a script at the old path that always recorded\n\".installed\", so a rewrite under that name would be filtered out on every\ninstall that already ran it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXfZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAo8YQAF7oM05CBaZUDyO1m/BykEWG\nZm1mpoc6dJbs4EI39d5X/+RGgKuL81/TmBGrLJ3rmG0tzkUC2omHM7NoKVs0C3kv\nc7QsNwYg36yFvUuFWvJZNKUSD+0kVrGdawvA+Z7upVDVHEAYIqiCuBUXmf6GyKCv\nb4pES1IeoTIOeViCkT1OaG8Egk9ytwR6XJYjseccznHKS1G8B58R0Q0xg9YRpWQ/\nWJsRS166do4jxNBSQ8mAfcBOK4mxGSNM4a5zJlxFMKkP+HYt4osopa+OVFNzax9d\n5lWczWRu44qQJdJBuWux9hIvXXk7cFLKPF29wuoZGl/8luGEgbmsUXv7eZ5qbsqX\nTuKAIJnY6rxylF92U3WJhd0EIDNoZSA5gjq3zMI+4AhuObRG4sI64jMZ7bGxim3L\nEpSTh3HgyhptePLE0DkSbfFVrY4VBjCr3WfVUfL9SAhDHycfRMFriWQ70OB2P1cb\nRBKCUJotdfNQvfK0fztCVP6JhBCpcIY7Wm1ohv4mUwiynoE1Izhs4fII+EvmqQc3\ncH+n2oTnYy1IDQkKqd2d/v3FeXD+flDkUW8TM06p/ia3ljJK+nB/JE8S3SbHgHuh\naZ8lBI8B18S79v/TTdUJeH8MVY0aH1fWzxoB8DojwSYNSN8+HJSGZAxMfsQP696N\nAzUHN/lVDxqgEbdiD3zh\n=JPms\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T12:47:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/6cc08b1cde144878d28e81ee0287879406dc5173","node_id":"C_kwDOCBq_hdoAKDZjYzA4YjFjZGUxNDQ4NzhkMjhlODFlZTAyODc4Nzk0MDZkYzUxNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcontent/commit/2a0341203a90f59a581569e0cd184a3ddc8579dc","sha":"2a0341203a90f59a581569e0cd184a3ddc8579dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/2a0341203a90f59a581569e0cd184a3ddc8579dc"}],"sha":"6cc08b1cde144878d28e81ee0287879406dc5173","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcontent/commits/6cc08b1cde144878d28e81ee0287879406dc5173"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75278792?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gflores-jahia","id":75278792,"login":"gflores-jahia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1Mjc4Nzky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gflores-jahia/received_eve